e surprised.\n\nNivel 17 - Thief's Reflexes\n\nPagina: 137\n\nYou are adept at laying ambushes and quickly escaping danger. You can take two turns during the first round of any combat. You take your first turn at your normal XPHB and your second turn at your XPHB minus 10."},
  ["feature.thief.xphb2024.rogue.thief.3"]={title="Thief",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 137\n\nHunt for Treasure as a Classic Adventurer\n\nA mix of burglar, treasure hunter, and explorer, you are the epitome of an adventurer. In addition to improving your agility and stealth, you gain abilities useful for delving into ruins and getting maximum benefit from the magic items you find there."},
  ["optionalfeature.thief-of-five-fates.phb2014"]={title="Thief of Five Fates",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 111\n\nYou can cast bane once using a warlock spell slot. You can't do so again until you finish a long rest."},
  ["feature.thief-s-reflexes.phb2014.rogue.thief.17"]={title="Thief's Reflexes",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 97\n\nWhen you reach 17th level, you have become adept at laying ambushes and quickly escaping danger. You can take two turns during the first round of any combat. You take your first turn at your normal initiative and your second turn at your initiative minus 10. You can't use this feature when you are surprised."},
  ["feature.thief-s-reflexes.xphb2024.rogue.thief.17"]={title="Thief's Reflexes",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 137\n\nYou are adept at laying ambushes and quickly escaping danger. You can take two turns during the first round of any combat. You take your first turn at your normal XPHB and your second turn at your XPHB minus 10."},
  ["magicitem.thief-s-thimble.au2014"]={title="Thief's Thimble",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 124\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis magic thimble aids thieves in foiling traps. While wearing this thimble, if you trigger a trap and take damage, the thimble takes the damage instead.\n\nThe thimble has 30 XPHB. If the thimble is reduced to 0 XPHB, it breaks, and you take any remaining damage."},
  ["language.thieves-cant.ggr2014"]={title="Thieves' Cant",subtitle="Idioma - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 9"},
  ["feature.thieves-cant.phb2014.rogue.base.1"]={title="Thieves' Cant",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["language.thieves-cant.phb2014"]={title="Thieves' Cant",subtitle="Idioma - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 94\n\nThieves' cant is a secret mix of dialect, jargon, and code that allows messages to be hidden in seemingly normal conversation. Only a creature that knows thieves' cant understands such messages. It takes four times longer to convey such a message than it does to speak the same idea plainly."},
  ["feature.thieves-cant.xphb2024.rogue.base.1"]={title="Thieves' Cant",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["language.thieves-cant.xphb2024"]={title="Thieves' Cant",subtitle="Idioma - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 37"},
  ["item.thieves-tools.phb2014"]={title="Thieves' Tools",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 154\n\nRaridade: none\n\nThis set of tools includes a small file, a set of lock picks, a small mirror mounted on a metal handle, a set of narrow-bladed scissors, and a pair of pliers. Proficiency with these tools lets you add your proficiency bonus to any ability checks you make to disarm traps or open locks.\n\nPerhaps the most common tools used by adventurers, thieves' tools are designed for picking locks and foiling traps. Proficiency with the tools also grants you a general knowledge of traps and locks.\n\nComponents\n\nThieves' tools include a small file, a set of lock picks, a small mirror mounted on a metal handle, a set of narrow-bladed scissors, and a pair of pliers.\n\nHistory\n\nYour knowledge of traps grants you insight when answering questions about locations that are renowned for their traps.\n\nInvestigation and Perception\n\nYou gain additional insight when looking for traps, because you have learned a variety of common signs that betray their presence.\n\nSet a Trap\n\nJust as you can disable traps, you can also set them. As part of a short rest, you can create a trap using items you have on hand. The total of your check becomes the DC for someone else's attempt to discover or disable the trap. The trap deals damage appropriate to the materials used in crafting it (such as poison or a weapon) or damage equal to half the total of your check, whichever the DM deems appropriate.\n\nActivity | DC\n\nPick a lock | Varies\n\nDisable a trap | Varies"},
  ["item.thieves-tools.xphb2024"]={title="Thieves' Tools",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 221\n\nRaridade: none\n\n• Ability: Dexterity\n\n• Utilize: Pick a lock (15), or disarm a trap (15)"},
  ["traphazard.thin-ice.dmg2014"]={title="Thin Ice",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 111\n\nThin ice has a weight tolerance of 3d10 × 10 pounds per 10-foot-square area. Whenever the total weight on an area of thin ice exceeds its tolerance, the ice in that area breaks. All creatures on broken ice fall through."},
  ["traphazard.thin-ice.xdmg2024"]={title="Thin Ice",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 69\n\nThin ice has a weight tolerance of 3d10 × 10 pounds per 10-foot-square area. Whenever the total weight on an area of thin ice exceeds its tolerance, the ice in that area breaks. All creatures on broken ice fall through. Below the ice is XDMG."},
  ["creature.thinnings.wbtw2014"]={title="Thinnings",subtitle="Criatura - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish, Sylvan"},
  ["psionic.third-eye.uathemysticclass2014"]={title="Third Eye",subtitle="Psionico - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 26\n\nYou create a third, psychic eye in your mind, which you cast out into the world. It channels thoughts and knowledge back to you, greatly enhancing your senses."},
  ["optionalfeature.thirsting-blade.phb2014"]={title="Thirsting Blade",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 111\n\nYou can attack with your pact weapon twice, instead of once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn."},
  ["optionalfeature.thirsting-blade.xphb2024"]={title="Thirsting Blade",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 157\n\nYou gain the Extra Attack feature for your pact weapon only. With that feature, you can attack twice with the weapon instead of once when you take the XPHB action on your turn."},
  ["creature.tholtz-daggerdark.skt2014"]={title="Tholtz Daggerdark",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 221\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.thomas-t-toad.rmbre2014"]={title="Thomas T. Toad",subtitle="Criatura - RMBRE - 2014",body="Pagina: 28\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 59 (7d10 + 21)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 8 | CON 16 | INT 5 | WIS 7 | CHA 7\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nWebby Hands\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.thopter-bat.psk2014"]={title="Thopter (Bat)",subtitle="Criatura - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, poisoned"},
  ["creature.thopter-blood-hawk.psk2014"]={title="Thopter (Blood Hawk)",subtitle="Criatura - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, poisoned"},
  ["creature.thopter-eagle.psk2014"]={title="Thopter (Eagle)",subtitle="Criatura - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, poisoned"},
  ["creature.thopter-hawk.psk2014"]={title="Thopter (Hawk)",subtitle="Criatura - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, poisoned"},
  ["creature.thopter-owl.psk2014"]={title="Thopter (Owl)",subtitle="Criatura - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, poisoned"},
  ["creature.thopter-pseudodragon.psk2014"]={title="Thopter (Pseudodragon)",subtitle="Criatura - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, poisoned"},
  ["creature.thopter-raven.psk2014"]={title="Thopter (Raven)",subtitle="Criatura - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, poisoned"},
  ["creature.thopter-vulture.psk2014"]={title="Thopter (Vulture)",subtitle="Criatura - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, poisoned"},
  ["deity.thor.phb2014"]={title="Thor",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 299"},
  ["creature.thorn-slinger.tftyp2014"]={title="Thorn Slinger",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 246\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / L\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 32 (5d10 + 5)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 12 | CON 12 | INT 1 | WIS 10 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, deafened, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAdhesive Blossoms\n\nThe thorn slinger adheres to anything that touches it. A Medium or smaller creature adhered to the thorn slinger is also grappled by it (escape 11). Ability checks made to escape this grapple have disadvantage.\n\nAt the end of each of the thorn slinger's turns, anything grappled by it takes 3 (1d6) acid damage.\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the thorn slinger remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from an inanimate bush.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nThorns\n\nmw,rw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30 ft., one target. h8 (2d6 + 1) piercing damage."},
  ["spell.thorn-whip.phb2014"]={title="Thorn Whip",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 282\n\nYou create a long, vine-like whip covered in thorns that lashes out at your command toward a creature in range. Make a melee spell attack against the target. If the attack hits, the creature takes 1d6 piercing damage, and if the creature is Large or smaller, you pull the creature up to 10 feet closer to you.\n\nThis spell's damage increases by 1d6 when you reach 5th level (2d6), 11th level (3d6), and 17th level (4d6)."},
  ["spell.thorn-whip.xphb2024"]={title="Thorn Whip",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 333\n\nYou create a vine-like whip covered in thorns that lashes out at your command toward a creature in range. Make a melee spell attack against the target. On a hit, the target takes 1d6 Piercing damage, and if it is Large or smaller, you can pull it up to 10 feet closer to you."},
  ["creature.thornboldt-thorn-durst.cos2014"]={title="Thornboldt \"Thorn\" Durst",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 217\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: S\n\nCR: 3\n\nPV: 35 (10d6)\n\nIdiomas: Common"},
  ["creature.thorny.vgm2014"]={title="Thorny",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 197\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 27 (5d8 + 5)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 12 | CON 13 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: lightning, piercing\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPlant Camouflage\n\nThe thorny has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks it makes in any terrain with ample obscuring plant life.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe thorny regains 5 hit points at the start of its turn. If it takes cold, fire, or necrotic damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of the thorny's next turn. The thorny dies only if it starts its turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\nThorny Body\n\nAt the start of its turn, the thorny deals 2 (1d4) piercing damage to any creature grappling it.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (2d6 + 1) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.thorny-vegepygmy.mpmm2014"]={title="Thorny Vegepygmy",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 253\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 27 (5d8 + 5)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 12 | CON 13 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: lightning, piercing\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPlant Camouflage\n\nThe thorny has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks it makes in any terrain with ample obscuring vegetation.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe thorny regains 5 hit points at the start of its turn. If it takes cold, fire, or necrotic damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of the thorny's next turn. The thorny dies only if it starts its turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\nThorny Body\n\nAt the start of its turn, the thorny deals 2 (1d4) piercing damage to any creature grappling it.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d8 + 1) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.thorvin-twinbeard.wdh2014"]={title="Thorvin Twinbeard",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 216\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 0\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 4 (1d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 25\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 10 | CON 10 | INT 10 | WIS 16 | CHA 10\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Dwarvish\n\nResistencias: poison\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDwarven Resilience\n\nThorvin has advantage on saving throws against poison and resistance to poison damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClub\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h2 (1d4) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["deity.thoth.phb2014"]={title="Thoth",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 299"},
  ["feature.thought-shield.phb2014.warlock.great-old-one.10"]={title="Thought Shield",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.thought-shield.xphb2024.warlock.great-old-one.10"]={title="Thought Shield",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["creature.thought-spy.ggr2014"]={title="Thought Spy",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 233\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 27 (6d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 16 | WIS 13 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common plus any one language\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCunning Action\n\nOn each of its turns, the thought spy can use a bonus action to take the Dash, Disengage, or Hide action.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe thought spy makes two melee attacks, or it makes three ranged attacks with its daggers.\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nRapier\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["feature.thousand-forms.phb2014.druid.moon.14"]={title="Thousand Forms",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 69\n\nBy 14th level, you have learned to use magic to alter your physical form in more subtle ways. You can cast the alter self spell at will."},
  ["creature.thousand-teeth.gos2014"]={title="Thousand Teeth",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 256\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 93 (11d10 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 50\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 10 | CON 17 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 7\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nHold Breath\n\nThousand Teeth can hold its breath for 30 minutes.\n\nLegendary Resistance (2/Day)\n\nIf Thousand Teeth fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThousand Teeth makes two attacks: one with its bite and one with its tail.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h15 (2d10 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 15 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThousand Teeth makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nLunge\n\nThousand Teeth moves up to half its speed.\n\nBite (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThousand Teeth makes a bite attack."},
  ["creature.thrakkus.wdh2014"]={title="Thrakkus",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 89\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 67 (9d8 + 27)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 12 | CON 17 | INT 9 | WIS 11 | CHA 9\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nResistencias: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nReckless\n\nAt the start of his turn, Thrakkus can gain advantage on all melee weapon attack rolls during that turn, but attack rolls against him have advantage until the start of his next turn.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nGreataxe\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d12 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nBreath Weapon (1/Day)\n\nThrakkus can use his action to exhale a 15-foot cone of fire. Each creature in the cone must make a 13 Dexterity saving throw, taking 6 (2d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.three-earrings.egw2014"]={title="Three Earrings",subtitle="Criatura - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 211\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["feature.three-extra-attacks.xphb2024.fighter.base.20"]={title="Three Extra Attacks",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 92\n\nYou can attack four times instead of once whenever you take the XPHB action on your turn."},
  ["magicitem.three-keyholes-dagger.au2014"]={title="Three Keyholes Dagger",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 128\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThree\n\nThree ornamental keyholes adorn the weapon's hilt.\n\nYou have a +1 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. When you take the XPHB action, you can transform this weapon into a XPHB or XPHB. It remains transformed in this way until the start of your next turn, at which point it reverts back to its XPHB form. Regardless of the weapon's form, you can use your choice of your Strength or Dexterity modifier for the attack and damage rolls; you must use the same modifier for both rolls."},
  ["item.three-dragon-ante-set.phb2014"]={title="Three-Dragon Ante Set",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 154\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.three-dragon-ante-set.xphb2024"]={title="Three-Dragon Ante Set",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 221\n\nRaridade: none\n\n• Ability: Wisdom\n\n• Utilize: Discern whether someone is cheating (10), or win the game (20)"},
  ["species.thri-kreen.aag2014"]={title="Thri-kreen",subtitle="Especie - AAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\nCreature Type\n\nYou are a Monstrosity.\n\nSize\n\nYou are Medium or Small. You choose the size when you select this race.\n\nChameleon Carapace\n\nWhile you aren't wearing armor, your carapace gives you a base Armor Class of 13 + your Dexterity modifier.\n\nAs an action, you can change the color of your carapace to match the color and texture of your surroundings, giving you advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide in those surroundings.\n\nDarkvision\n\nYou can see in dim light within 60 feet of yourself as if it were bright light, and in darkness as if it were dim light. You discern colors in that darkness only as shades of gray.\n\nSecondary Arms\n\nYou have two slightly smaller secondary arms below your primary pair of arms. The secondary arms can manipulate an object, open or close a door or container, pick up or set down a Tiny object, or wield a weapon that has the L property.\n\nSleepless\n\nYou do not require sleep and can remain conscious during a long rest, though you must still refrain from strenuous activity to gain the benefit of the rest.\n\nThri-kreen Telepathy\n\nWithout the assistance of magic, you can't speak the non-thri-kreen languages you know. Instead you use telepathy to convey your thoughts. You have the magical ability to transmit your thoughts mentally to willing creatures within 120 feet of yourself. A contacted creature doesn't need to share a language with you to understand your thoughts, but it must be able to understand at least one language. Your telepathic link to a creature is broken if you and the creature move more than 120 feet apart, if either of you is incapacitated, or if either of you mentally breaks the contact (no action required)."},
  ["creature.thri-kreen.mm2014"]={title="Thri-kreen",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 288\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 15 | CON 13 | INT 8 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Thri-kreen\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nChameleon Carapace\n\nThe thri-kreen can change the color of its carapace to match the color and texture of its surroundings. As a result, it has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide.\n\nStanding Leap\n\nThe thri-kreen's long jump is up to 30 feet and its high jump is up to 15 feet, with or without a running start.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe thri-kreen makes two attacks: one with its bite and one with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h4 (1d6 + 1) piercing damage, and the target must succeed on a 11 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned for 1 minute. If the saving throw fails by 5 or more, the target is also paralyzed while poisoned in this way. The poisoned target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (2d4 + 1) slashing damage."},
  ["language.thri-kreen.mm2014"]={title="Thri-kreen",subtitle="Idioma - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 288"},
  ["language.thri-kreen.xmm2024"]={title="Thri-kreen",subtitle="Idioma - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 306"},
  ["creature.thri-kreen-gladiator.bam2014"]={title="Thri-kreen Gladiator",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 60\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 142 (19d8 + 57)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 18 | CON 16 | INT 10 | WIS 15 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: telepathy 60 ft., Thri-kreen\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe thri-kreen makes two Gythka attacks and one Chatkcha attack.\n\nGythka\n\nmw 7 to hit (with advantage if the thri-kreen is missing any hit points), reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nChatkcha\n\nrw 7 to hit (with advantage if the thri-kreen is missing any hit points), range 30/120 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) slashing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nLeap\n\nThe thri-kreen leaps up to 20 feet in any direction, provided its speed isn't 0.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nThe thri-kreen adds 3 to its AC against one melee attack that would hit it. To do so, the thri-kreen must see the attacker and be wielding a melee weapon."},
  ["creature.thri-kreen-hunter.bam2014"]={title="Thri-kreen Hunter",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 61\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 60 (11d8 + 11)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 16 | CON 13 | INT 10 | WIS 14 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: telepathy 60 ft., Thri-kreen\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe thri-kreen makes two Gythka or Chatkcha attacks.\n\nGythka\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nChatkcha\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 30/120 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) slashing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChameleon Carapace\n\nThe thri-kreen changes the color of its carapace to match the color and texture of its surroundings, gaining advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks it makes to hide in those surroundings.\n\nLeap\n\nThe thri-kreen leaps up to 20 feet in any direction, provided its speed isn't 0.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nThe thri-kreen adds 2 to its AC against one melee attack that would hit it. To do so, the thri-kreen must see the attacker and be wielding a melee weapon."},
  ["creature.thri-kreen-marauder.xmm2024"]={title="Thri-kreen Marauder",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 306\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 15 | CON 13 | INT 8 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Thri-kreen; telepathy 60 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe thri-kreen makes two attacks, using Gythka or Chatkcha in any combination.\n\nGythka\n\nm 3, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d8 + 1) Slashing damage plus 2 (1d4) Poison damage.\n\nChatkcha\n\nr 4, range 30/120 ft. h5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nLeap\n\nThe thri-kreen jumps up to 15 feet by spending 5 feet of movement."},
  ["creature.thri-kreen-mystic.bam2014"]={title="Thri-kreen Mystic",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 61\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 99 (18d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 15 | CON 13 | INT 12 | WIS 16 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: telepathy 60 ft., Thri-kreen\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe thri-kreen makes two Gythka attacks or four Psychic Bolt attacks.\n\nGythka\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d8 + 1) slashing damage.\n\nPsychic Bolt\n\nrs 6 to hit, range 60 ft., one creature. h6 (1d6 + 3) psychic damage.\n\nDrain Vitality (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe thri-kreen targets one creature it can see within 30 feet of itself. The target must make a 14 Constitution saving throw, taking 32 (5d12) necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. The thri-kreen regains hit points equal to the damage dealt.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChameleon Carapace\n\nThe thri-kreen changes the color of its carapace to match the color and texture of its surroundings, gaining advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks it makes to hide in those surroundings."},
  ["creature.thri-kreen-psion.xmm2024"]={title="Thri-kreen Psion",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 306\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 149 (23d8 + 46)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 20\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 15 | CON 14 | INT 19 | WIS 12 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Thri-kreen; telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: psychic\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe thri-kreen makes three Psionic Lance attacks.\n\nPsionic Lance\n\nm,r 7, reach 10 ft. or range 120 ft. h18 (4d6 + 4) Psychic damage."},
  ["magicitem.throne-card.bmt2014"]={title="Throne Card",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nAs an action, you can speak a command word while holding this card to gain advantage on Charisma (Intimidation or Persuasion) checks for 1 minute. In addition, for that duration, you can use this card to cast the Command spell (save 17) as an action. Once this property is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["optionalfeature.thrown-weapon-fighting.tce2014"]={title="Thrown Weapon Fighting",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\nYou can draw a weapon that has the thrown property as part of the attack you make with the weapon.\n\nIn addition, when you hit with a ranged attack using a thrown weapon, you gain a +2 bonus to the damage roll."},
  ["feat.thrown-weapon-fighting.xphb2024"]={title="Thrown Weapon Fighting",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 210\n\nWhen you hit with a ranged attack roll using a weapon that has the XPHB property, you gain a +2 bonus to the damage roll."},
  ["deity.thrym.phb2014"]={title="Thrym",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 299"},
  ["traphazard.thrym-s-howl.tce2014"]={title="Thrym's Howl",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 163\n\nThese bone-chilling blizzards drive a wall of wind and snow like a living glacier. The storm projects extreme cold (see the DMG). Due to the howling wind and dense blue-white ice particles, the area in the storm is heavily obscured, and ranged attack rolls and Wisdom (Perception) checks made within it have disadvantage.\n\nAny creature exposed to the storm at the start of its turn takes 2d6 cold damage and can't regain hit points until it spends at least 1 hour in a warm environment. A creature that dies in the storm freezes solid. Creatures that are immune to cold damage are immune to the effects of the storm and can see normally within it.\n\nThrym's howl typically lasts 2d10 hours."},
  ["creature.thug.mm2014"]={title="Thug",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 350\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 32 (5d8 + 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 11 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe thug has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the thug's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe thug makes two melee attacks.\n\nMace\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h5 (1d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage.\n\nHeavy Crossbow\n\nrw 2 to hit, range 100/400 ft., one target. h5 (1d10) piercing damage."},
  ["magicitem.thunder-absorbing-tattoo.tce2014"]={title="Thunder Absorbing Tattoo",subtitle="Item Magico - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\n{#itemEntry Absorbing Tattoo|TCE"},
  ["feature.thunder-gauntlets.tce2014.artificer.armorer.3"]={title="Thunder Gauntlets",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["spell.thunder-step.xge2024"]={title="Thunder Step",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 168\n\nYou teleport yourself to an unoccupied space you can see within range. Immediately after you disappear, a thunderous boom sounds, and each creature within 10 feet of the space you left must make a Constitution saving throw, taking 3d10 thunder damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. The thunder can be heard from up to 300 feet away.\n\nYou can bring along objects as long as their weight doesn't exceed what you can carry. You can also teleport one willing creature of your size or smaller who is carrying gear up to its carrying capacity. The creature must be within 5 feet of you when you cast this spell, and there must be an unoccupied space within 5 feet of your destination space for the creature to appear in; otherwise, the creature is left behind."},
  ["creature.thunderbeast-skeleton.skt2014"]={title="Thunderbeast Skeleton",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 99\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / H\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 68 (8d12 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 11 | CON 15 | INT 2 | WIS 12 | CHA 5\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: bludgeoning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned, exhaustion\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., h18 (4d6 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nTail\n\n7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h18 (4d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage. Succeed on a DC14 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone."},
  ["feature.thunderbolt-strike.phb2014.cleric.tempest.6"]={title="Thunderbolt Strike",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 62\n\nAt 6th level, when you deal lightning damage to a Large or smaller creature, you can also push it up to 10 feet away from you."},
  ["magicitem.thunderbuss.bgg2014"]={title="Thunderbuss",subtitle="Item Magico - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 116\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis magic ranged weapon is a flared pistol with the storm rune engraved along the barrel. You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. It requires no ammunition, its damage is thunder instead of piercing, and it doesn't have the loading property.\n\nInvoking the Rune\n\nAs a bonus action, you can invoke the weapon's rune to launch a ball of energy to a point you can see within 30 feet of yourself. The energy then detonates into a 10-foot-radius sphere of turbulent wind and thunder centered on that point, and each creature in that sphere must make a 14 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 3d6 thunder damage, and it can't take reactions until the end of your next turn. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage only.\n\nOnce the rune has been invoked, it can't be invoked again until the next dawn."},
  ["spell.thunderclap.xge2024"]={title="Thunderclap",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 168\n\nYou create a burst of thunderous sound that can be heard up to 100 feet away. Each creature within range, other than you, must make a Constitution saving throw or take 1d6 thunder damage.\n\nThe spell's damage increases by 1d6 when you reach 5th level (2d6), 11th level (3d6), and 17th level (4d6)."},
  ["spell.thunderclap.xphb2024"]={title="Thunderclap",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 333\n\nEach creature in a 5-foot XPHB originating from you must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or take 1d6 Thunder damage. The spell's thunderous sound can be heard up to 100 feet away."},
  ["magicitem.thunderous-greatclub.xdmg2024"]={title="Thunderous Greatclub",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 316\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile you are attuned to this magic weapon, your Strength is 20 unless your Strength is already equal to or greater than that score. The weapon deals an extra 1d8 Thunder damage to any creature it hits and an extra 3d8 Thunder damage to objects it hits that aren't being worn or carried.\n\nThe weapon has the following additional properties.\n\nClap of Thunder\n\nAs a XPHB action, you can strike the weapon against a hard surface to create a loud clap of thunder audible out to 300 feet. You also create a 30-foot XPHB of thunderous energy. Each creature in the XPHB must succeed on a 15 Strength saving throw or have the XPHB condition. Nonmagical objects in the XPHB that aren't being worn or carried take 3d8 Thunder damage.\n\nEarthquake\n\nAs a XPHB action, you can strike the weapon against the ground to create an intense seismic disturbance in a 50-foot-radius circle centered on the point of impact. Structures in contact with the ground in that area take 50 Bludgeoning damage, and each creature on the ground in that area must succeed on a 20 Dexterity saving throw or have the XPHB condition. If that creature is also XPHB, it must succeed on a 20 Constitution saving throw or its XPHB is broken. In addition, you can cause a 30-foot-deep, 10-foot-wide fissure to open up on the ground anywhere in the area. Any creature on a spot where the fissure opens must make a 20 Dexterity saving throw, falling into the fissure on a failed save or moving with the fissure's edge on a successful one. Any structure on a spot where the fissure opens collapses into the fissure. Once you use this property, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["spell.thunderous-smite.phb2014"]={title="Thunderous Smite",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 282\n\nThe first time you hit with a melee weapon attack during this spell's duration, your weapon rings with thunder that is audible within 300 feet of you, and the attack deals an extra 2d6 thunder damage to the target. Additionally, if the target is a creature, it must succeed on a Strength saving throw or be pushed 10 feet away from you and knocked prone."},
  ["spell.thunderous-smite.xphb2024"]={title="Thunderous Smite",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 334\n\nYour strike rings with thunder that is audible within 300 feet of you, and the target takes an extra 2d6 Thunder damage from the attack. Additionally, if the target is a creature, it must succeed on a Strength saving throw or be pushed 10 feet away from you and have the XPHB condition."},
  ["spell.thunderwave.phb2014"]={title="Thunderwave",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 282\n\nA wave of thunderous force sweeps out from you. Each creature in a 15-foot cube originating from you must make a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 2d8 thunder damage and is pushed 10 feet away from you. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't pushed.\n\nIn addition, unsecured objects that are completely within the area of effect are automatically pushed 10 feet away from you by the spell's effect, and the spell emits a thunderous boom audible out to 300 feet."},
  ["spell.thunderwave.xphb2024"]={title="Thunderwave",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 334\n\nYou unleash a wave of thunderous energy. Each creature in a 15-foot XPHB originating from you makes a Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 2d8 Thunder damage and is pushed 10 feet away from you. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage only.\n\nIn addition, unsecured objects that are entirely within the XPHB are pushed 10 feet away from you, and a thunderous boom is audible within 300 feet."},
  ["creature.thurl-merosska.pota2014"]={title="Thurl Merosska",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 192\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 71 (11d8 + 21)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 11 | WIS 10 | CHA 15\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Auran, Common\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThurl makes two melee attacks.\n\nGreatsword\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d6 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nLance\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h9 (1d12 + 3) piercing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nThurl adds 2 to his AC against one melee attack that would hit him. To do so, Thurl must see the attacker and be wielding a melee weapon."},
  ["creature.thurstwell-vanthampur.bgdia2014"]={title="Thurstwell Vanthampur",subtitle="Criatura - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 9\n\nPV: 5 (2d8 - 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 7 | DEX 8 | CON 6 | INT 15 | WIS 17 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish, Infernal\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDark Devotion\n\nThurstwell has advantage on saving throws against being charmed or frightened.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSacred Flame (Cantrip)\n\nFlame-like radiance descends on one creature Thurstwell can see within 60 feet of him. The target must succeed on a 13 Dexterity saving throw or take 4 (1d8) radiant damage, gaining no benefit from cover."},
  ["creature.thwad-underbrew.wdmm2014"]={title="Thwad Underbrew",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 204\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nIdiomas: Common, Dwarvish"},
  ["deity.tiamat.dmg2014"]={title="Tiamat",subtitle="Divindade - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 10"},
  ["deity.tiamat.egw2014"]={title="Tiamat",subtitle="Divindade - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 28\n\nThe evil queen of dragons is a fearsome god of greed, envy, and hoarded wealth. While chromatic dragons are her foremost worshipers, Tiamat accepts the worship of any who crave wealth. All chromatic dragons have a fearful reverence for their tyrannical queen, but many dragons of near-deific power and ambition chafe under her rule.\n\nTiamat remains imprisoned in Avernus, the first of the Nine Hells, influencing the souls of chromatic dragons across the planes and seeking the means to free herself.\n\nDepiction\n\nMost representations of Tiamat exist as warnings within sanctuaries of the Platinum Dragon Bahamut. She is shown as a drake of frightful size, with massive leathery wings spreading clouds of poisonous mist, while she shouts from five vicious dragon heads, each one a chromatic color of her evil children.\n\nEnemies\n\nThe Scaled Tyrant's hatred for Bahamut is as old as the Founding, and her cults are ever hunted by his justice. For centuries, the zealous paladins of Bahamut have limited her worship to the chromatic dragons, but a rise in cult activity in the underbelly of Dwendalian society has priests of the Platinum Dragon on edge.\n\nCommandments of Tiamat\n\n• Amass wealth, but spend little. The gold—and the power that comes with it—is sufficient reward in itself.\n\n• Do not forgive nor forget an indignity to yourself. Let no affront go unpunished.\n\n• Take what you covet. Those without the strength to defend their dominion are not worthy to have one."},
  ["deity.tiamat.phb2014"]={title="Tiamat",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 296"},
  ["creature.tiamat.rot2014"]={title="Tiamat",subtitle="Criatura - RoT - 2014",body="Pagina: 92\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / G\n\nCR: 30\n\nCA: 25\n\nPV: 615 (30d20 + 300)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, fly: 120\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 10 | CON 30 | INT 26 | WIS 26 | CHA 28\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 240 ft., truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Infernal\n\nImunidades: acid, cold, fire, lightning, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, frightened, poisoned, stunned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDiscorporation\n\nWhen Tiamat drops to 0 hit points or dies, her body is destroyed but her essence travels back to her domain in the Nine Hells, and she is unable to take physical form for a time.\n\nLegendary Resistance (5/Day)\n\nIf Tiamat fails a saving throw, she can choose to succeed instead.\n\nLimited Magic Immunity\n\nUnless she wishes to be affected, Tiamat is immune to spells of 6th level or lower. She has advantage on saving throws against all other spells and magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nTiamat's weapon attacks are magical.\n\nMultiple Heads\n\nTiamat can take one reaction per turn, rather than only one per round. She also has advantage on saving throws against being knocked unconscious. If she fails a saving throw against an effect that would stun a creature, one of her unspent legendary actions is spent.\n\nRegeneration\n\nTiamat regains 30 hit points at the start of her turn.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nTiamat can use her Frightful Presence. She then makes three attacks: two with her claws and one with her tail.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 19 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h24 (4d6 + 10) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 19 to hit, reach 25 ft., one target. h28 (4d8 + 10) piercing damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of Tiamat's choice that is within 240 feet of Tiamat and aware of her must succeed on a 26 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to Tiamat's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 19 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h32 (4d10 + 10) slashing damage plus 14 (4d6) acid damage (black dragon head), lightning damage (blue dragon head), poison damage (green dragon head), fire damage (red dragon head), or cold damage (white dragon head).\n\nBlack Dragon Head: Acid Breath (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nTiamat breathes acid in a 120-foot line that is 10 feet wide. Each creature in that line must make a 27 Dexterity saving throw, taking 67 (15d8) acid damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nBlue Dragon Head: Lightning Breath (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nTiamat breathes lightning in a 120-foot line that is 10 feet wide. Each creature in that line must make a 27 Dexterity saving throw, taking 88 (16d10) lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nGreen Dragon Head: Poison Breath (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nTiamat breathes poisonous gas in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 27 Constitution saving throw, taking 77 (22d6) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nRed Dragon Head: Fire Breath (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nTiamat breathes fire in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 27 Dexterity saving throw, taking 91 (26d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nWhite Dragon Head: Cold Breath (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nTiamat breathes an icy blast in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 27 Dexterity saving throw, taking 72 (16d8) cold damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.tiax.coa2014"]={title="Tiax",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 266\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 13/16\n\nPV: 110 (20d6 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 25\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 16 | CON 14 | INT 15 | WIS 19 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Gnomish\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nGnome Cunning\n\nTiax has advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma saving throws against magic.\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nTiax wears a Ring of Resistance that grants him resistance to radiant damage.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nTouch of Decay\n\nms 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h37 (6d10 + 4) necrotic damage.\n\nUnholy Firebolt\n\nTiax causes unholy fire to flare up in a creature's space within 60 feet of him. The target must succeed on a 16 Dexterity saving throw or take 18 (4d8) necrotic damage plus 18 (4d8) poison damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nHeal (2/Day)\n\nTiax heals 70 hit points."},
  ["creature.tiberius-inuus.mabjov2014"]={title="Tiberius Inuus",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 44\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 170 (20d8 + 80)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 12 | CON 18 | INT 11 | WIS 11 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBrave\n\nTiberius Inuus has advantage on saving throws against being frightened.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nTiberius Inuus makes three Flame Tongue attacks.\n\nFlame Tongue\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) fire damage.\n\nHeavy Crossbow\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 100/400 ft., one target. h6 (1d10 + 1) piercing damage.\n\nTouch of Sune\n\nTiberius Inuus touches a creature. The target magically regains 40 hit points and is freed from any disease or poison.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nVengeance\n\nWhen Tiberius Inuus is hit by an attack he can utter an oath of vengeance against the creature that made the attack. He gains advantage on attack rolls against that creature for 1 minute or until it drops to 0 hit points or falls unconscious."},
  ["spell.tidal-wave.xge2024"]={title="Tidal Wave",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 168\n\nYou conjure up a wave of water that crashes down on an area within range. The area can be up to 30 feet long, up to 10 feet wide, and up to 10 feet tall. Each creature in that area must make a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 4d8 bludgeoning damage and is knocked prone. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage and isn't knocked prone. The water then spreads out across the ground in all directions, extinguishing unprotected flames in its area and within 30 feet of it, and then it vanishes."},
  ["magicitem.tidecaller-trident.bmt2014"]={title="Tidecaller Trident",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 69\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nYou gain a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic trident. You also have advantage on attack rolls made with this weapon while underwater.\n\nThis trident has 3 charges. You can expend 1 charge to cast Control Water (save 15) from the trident or 3 charges to cast Tsunami (save 15) from it instead. The trident regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn."},
  ["feature.tides-of-chaos.phb2014.sorcerer.wild.1"]={title="Tides of Chaos",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 103\n\nStarting at 1st level, you can manipulate the forces of chance and chaos to gain advantage on one attack roll, ability check, or saving throw. Once you do so, you must finish a long rest before you can use this feature again.\n\nAny time before you regain the use of this feature, the DM can have you roll on the PHB table immediately after you cast a sorcerer spell of 1st level or higher. You then regain the use of this feature."},
  ["feature.tides-of-chaos.xphb2024.sorcerer.wild-magic.3"]={title="Tides of Chaos",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 149\n\nYou can manipulate chaos itself to give yourself XPHB on one XPHB before you roll the d20. Once you do so, you must cast a Sorcerer spell with a spell slot or finish a XPHB before you can use this feature again.\n\nIf you do cast a Sorcerer spell with a spell slot before you finish a XPHB, you automatically roll on the XPHB table."},
  ["species.tiefling.phb2014"]={title="Tiefling",subtitle="Especie - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\nAge\n\nTieflings mature at the same rate as humans but live a few years longer.\n\nSize\n\nTieflings are about the same size and build as humans. Your size is Medium.\n\nDarkvision\n\nThanks to your infernal heritage, you have superior vision in dark and dim conditions. You can see in dim light within 60 feet of you as if it were bright light, and in darkness as if it were dim light. You can't discern color in darkness, only shades of gray.\n\nHellish Resistance\n\nYou have resistance to fire damage.\n\nInfernal Legacy\n\nYou know the thaumaturgy cantrip. Once you reach 3rd level, you can cast the hellish rebuke spell as a 2nd-level spell with this trait; you regain the ability to cast it when you finish a long rest. Once you reach 5th level, you can also cast the darkness spell once per day with this trait; you regain the ability to cast it when you finish a long rest. Charisma is your spellcasting ability for these spells.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and Infernal."},
  ["species.tiefling.xphb2024"]={title="Tiefling",subtitle="Especie - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 197\n\nDarkvision\n\nYou have XPHB with a range of 60 feet.\n\nFiendish Legacy\n\nYou are the recipient of a legacy that grants you supernatural abilities. Choose a legacy from the Fiendish Legacies table. You gain the level 1 benefit of the chosen legacy.\n\nWhen you reach character levels 3 and 5, you learn a higher-level spell, as shown on the table. You always have that spell prepared. You can cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in that way when you finish a XPHB. You can also cast the spell using any spell slots you have of the appropriate level. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for the spells you cast with this trait (choose the ability when you select the legacy).\n\nLegacy | Level 1 | Level 3 | Level 5\n\nAbyssal | You have XPHB to Poison damage. You also know the XPHB cantrip. | XPHB | XPHB\n\nChthonic | You have XPHB to Necrotic damage. You also know the XPHB cantrip. | XPHB | XPHB\n\nInfernal | You have XPHB to Fire damage. You also know the XPHB cantrip. | XPHB | XPHB\n\nOtherworldly Presence\n\nYou know the XPHB cantrip. When you cast it with this trait, the spell uses the same spellcasting ability you use for your Fiendish Legacy Trait."},
  ["creature.tiefling-acrobat.kftgv2014"]={title="Tiefling Acrobat",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 37\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nPericias:"},
  ["creature.tiefling-muralist.imr2014"]={title="Tiefling Muralist",subtitle="Criatura - IMR - 2014",body="Pagina: 17\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.tiger.mm2014"]={title="Tiger",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 339\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 37 (5d10 + 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 15 | CON 14 | INT 3 | WIS 12 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Smell\n\nThe tiger has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.\n\nPounce\n\nIf the tiger moves at least 20 feet straight toward a creature and then hits it with a claw attack on the same turn, that target must succeed on a 13 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone. If the target is prone, the tiger can make one bite attack against it as a bonus action.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d10 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) slashing damage."},
  ["feature.tiger.scag2014.barbarian.totem-warrior.3"]={title="Tiger",subtitle="Caracteristica - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 122\n\nWhile raging, you can add 10 feet to your long jump distance and 3 feet to your high jump distance. The spirit of the tiger empowers your leaps."},
  ["feature.tiger.scag2014.barbarian.totem-warrior.6"]={title="Tiger",subtitle="Caracteristica - SCAG - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.tiger.scag2014.barbarian.totem-warrior.14"]={title="Tiger",subtitle="Caracteristica - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 122\n\nWhile you're raging, if you move at least 20 feet in a straight line toward a Large or smaller target right before making a melee weapon attack against it, you can use a bonus action to make an additional melee weapon attack against it."},
  ["creature.tiger.xmm2024"]={title="Tiger",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 371\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 30 (4d10 + 8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 16 | CON 14 | INT 3 | WIS 12 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nRend\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h10 (2d6 + 3) Slashing damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nNimble Escape\n\nThe tiger takes the XPHB or XPHB action."},
  ["item.tiger-eye.dmg2014"]={title="Tiger Eye",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA translucent brown with golden center gemstone."},
  ["item.tiger-eye.xdmg2024"]={title="Tiger Eye",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA brown with golden center gemstone."},
  ["creature.timbermaw.psz2014"]={title="Timbermaw",subtitle="Criatura - PSZ - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.time-dragon-wyrmling.mpp2014"]={title="Time Dragon Wyrmling",subtitle="Criatura - MPP - 2014",body="Pagina: 51\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 75 (10d8 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30, fly: 60\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 10 | CON 17 | INT 17 | WIS 13 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 10 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic plus any two languages\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) force damage.\n\nTime Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a wave of shimmering light in a 15-foot cone. Nonmagical objects and vegetation in that area that aren't being worn or carried crumble to dust. Each creature in that area must make a 14 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 27 (6d8) force damage and is magically weakened as it is desynchronized from the time stream. While the creature is in this state, attack rolls against it have advantage. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage only. A weakened creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["reward.time-of-the-dragon.tofw2014"]={title="Time of the Dragon",subtitle="Recompensa - ToFW - 2014",body="Pagina: 68\n\nWhile holding the scale, you can use an action to summon Renesnuprah, an MPP (see MPP). The dragon appears in an unoccupied space of your choice that you can see within 60 feet of you and aids you for 10 minutes. Afterward, the time dragon vanishes, and the scale crumbles."},
  ["spell.time-ravage.egw2014"]={title="Time Ravage",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 9 - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 189\n\nYou target a creature you can see within range, putting its physical form through the devastation of rapid aging. The target must make a Constitution saving throw, taking 10d12 necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. If the save fails, the target also ages to the point where it has only 30 days left before it dies of old age. In this aged state, the target has disadvantage on attack rolls, ability checks, and saving throws, and its walking speed is halved. Only the wish spell or the greater restoration cast with a 9th-level spell slot can end these effects and restore the target to its previous age."},
  ["spell.time-stop.phb2014"]={title="Time Stop",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 9 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 283\n\nYou briefly stop the flow of time for everyone but yourself. No time passes for other creatures, while you take 1d4 + 1 turns in a row, during which you can use actions and move as normal.\n\nThis spell ends if one of the actions you use during this period, or any effects that you create during this period, affects a creature other than you or an object being worn or carried by someone other than you. In addition, the spell ends if you move to a place more than 1,000 feet from the location where you cast it."},
  ["spell.time-stop.xphb2024"]={title="Time Stop",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 9 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 334\n\nYou briefly stop the flow of time for everyone but yourself. No time passes for other creatures, while you take 1d4 + 1 turns in a row, during which you can use actions and move as normal.\n\nThis spell ends if one of the actions you use during this period, or any effects that you create during it, affects a creature other than you or an object being worn or carried by someone other than you. In addition, the spell ends if you move to a place more than 1,000 feet from the location where you cast it."},
  ["feature.timeless-body.phb2014.druid.base.18"]={title="Timeless Body",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 64\n\nStarting at 18th level, the primal magic that you wield causes you to age more slowly. For every 10 years that pass, your body ages only 1 year."},
  ["feature.timeless-body.phb2014.monk.base.15"]={title="Timeless Body",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 76\n\nAt 15th level, your ki sustains you so that you suffer none of the frailty of old age, and you can't be aged magically. You can still die of old age, however. In addition, you no longer need food or water."},
  ["magicitem.timepiece-of-travel.ai2014"]={title="Timepiece of Travel",subtitle="Item Magico - AI - 2014",body="Pagina: 221\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile attuned to this device, you have a +1 bonus to Dexterity saving throws and you always know which way is north. Additionally, you can cast the longstrider spell on yourself at will.\n\nTurn-by-Turn Directions\n\nYou can name any location within 10 miles of your current location that is known to at least one creature also within 10 miles of that location (including you). Once you name the location, a disembodied voice heard only by you provides directions to the location by the safest, most direct route. The voice knows to avoid natural hazards, so that it does not send you through trackless wilderness or into a lake. But it has no knowledge of or ability to help you avoid monsters, enemies, traps, locked doors, and the like.\n\nThe timepiece is of no use for reaching locations that are wholly secret or not known to any creatures within range. Once you use this feature of the timepiece of travel, it cannot be used again until the next dawn.\n\nGet Away From It All\n\nAs an action, you can cast the teleport spell. Once you use this feature of the timepiece of travel, it cannot be used again until the next dawn.\n\nPart of a Whole\n\nWhile this component is not installed in the AI, its magic might function sporadically or with unpredictable side effects, as determined by the DM."},
  ["creature.tin-soldier.wbtw2014"]={title="Tin Soldier",subtitle="Criatura - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 115\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / S\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 27 (6d6 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 25\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 11 | CON 13 | INT 1 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAntimagic Susceptibility\n\nThe tin soldier is incapacitated while in the area of an antimagic field. If targeted by dispel magic, the tin soldier must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against the caster's spell save DC or fall unconscious for 1 minute.\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the tin soldier remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from a normal suit of armor.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe tin soldier makes two melee attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["item.tinderbox.phb2014"]={title="Tinderbox",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 153\n\nRaridade: none\n\nThis small container holds flint, fire steel, and tinder (usually dry cloth soaked in light oil) used to kindle a fire. Using it to light a torch—or anything else with abundant, exposed fuel—takes an action. Lighting any other fire takes 1 minute."},
  ["item.tinderbox.xphb2024"]={title="Tinderbox",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 229\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA Tinderbox is a small container holding flint, fire steel, and tinder (usually dry cloth soaked in light oil) used to kindle a fire. Using it to light a XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB—or anything else with exposed fuel—takes a XPHB. Lighting any other fire takes 1 minute."},
  ["magicitem.tinderstrike.pota2014"]={title="Tinderstrike",subtitle="Item Magico - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 224\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nA flint dagger, Tinderstrike is uncommonly sharp, and sparks cascade off its edge whenever it strikes something solid. Its handle is always warm to the touch, and the blade smolders for 1d4 minutes after it is used to deal damage. It contains a spark of PotA, Prince of Evil Fire.\n\nYou gain a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. When you hit with it, the target takes an extra 2d6 fire damage.\n\nFire Mastery\n\nYou gain the following benefits while you hold Tinderstrike:\n\n• You can speak Ignan fluently.\n\n• You have resistance to fire damage.\n\n• You can cast dominate monster (save 17) on a fire elemental. Once you have done so, Tinderstrike can't be used this way again until the next dawn.\n\nDance of the All-Consuming Fire\n\nWhile inside a fire node, you can perform a ritual called the Dance of the All-Consuming Fire, using Tinderstrike to create a PotA. Once you perform the ritual, Tinderstrike can't be used to perform the ritual again until the next dawn.\n\nFlaw\n\nTinderstrike makes its wielder impatient and rash. While attuned to the weapon, you gain the following flaw: \"I act without thinking and take risks without weighing the consequences.\""},
  ["feature.tinker-s-magic.efa2014.artificer.base.1"]={title="Tinker's Magic",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\nYou know the XPHB cantrip.\n\nAs a XPHB action while holding XPHB, you can create one item in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of yourself, choosing the item from the following list:\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\nSee the rules for the item in the XPHB. The item lasts until you finish a XPHB, at which point it vanishes.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB."},
  ["item.tinker-s-tools.phb2014"]={title="Tinker's Tools",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 154\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA set of tinker's tools is designed to enable you to repair many mundane objects. Though you can't manufacture much with tinker's tools, you can mend torn clothes, sharpen a worn sword, and patch a tattered suit of chain mail.\n\nComponents\n\nTinker's tools include a variety of hand tools, thread, needles, a whetstone, scraps of cloth and leather, and a small pot of glue.\n\nHistory\n\nYou can determine the age and origin of objects, even if you have only a few pieces remaining from the original.\n\nInvestigation\n\nWhen you inspect a damaged object, you gain knowledge of how it was damaged and how long ago.\n\nRepair\n\nYou can restore 10 hit points to a damaged object for each hour of work. For any object, you need access to the raw materials required to repair it. For metal objects, you need access to an open flame hot enough to make the metal pliable.\n\nActivity | DC\n\nTemporarily repair a disabled device | 10\n\nRepair an item in half the time | 15\n\nImprovise a temporary item using scraps | 20"},
  ["item.tinker-s-tools.xphb2024"]={title="Tinker's Tools",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 221\n\nRaridade: none\n\n• Ability: Dexterity\n\n• Utilize: Assemble a Tiny item composed of scrap, which falls apart in 1 minute (20)\n\n• Craft: XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB"},
  ["item.tiny-jade-figurine-river-heralds.psx2014"]={title="Tiny jade figurine (River Heralds)",subtitle="Item - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["spell.tiny-servant.xge2024"]={title="Tiny Servant",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 168\n\nYou touch one Tiny, nonmagical object that isn't attached to another object or a surface and isn't being carried by another creature. The target animates and sprouts little arms and legs, becoming a creature under your control until the spell ends or the creature drops to 0 hit points. See the xge for its statistics.\n\nAs a bonus action, you can mentally command the creature if it is within 120 feet of you. (If you control multiple creatures with this spell, you can command any or all of them at the same time, issuing the same command to each one.) You decide what action the creature will take and where it will move during its next turn, or you can issue a simple, general command, such as to fetch a key, stand watch, or stack some books. If you issue no commands, the servant does nothing other than defend itself against hostile creatures. Once given an order, the servant continues to follow that order until its task is complete.\n\nWhen the creature drops to 0 hit points, it reverts to its original form, and any remaining damage carries over to that form."},
  ["creature.tiny-servant.xge2024"]={title="Tiny Servant",subtitle="Criatura - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 169\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / T\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 10 (4d4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 4 | DEX 16 | CON 10 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["feature.tipsy-sway.xge2024.monk.drunken-master.6"]={title="Tipsy Sway",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 33\n\nStarting at 6th level, you can move in sudden, swaying ways. You gain the following benefits."},
  ["feature.tireless.xphb2024.ranger.base.10"]={title="Tireless",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["feat.tireless-reveler.abh2014"]={title="Tireless Reveler",subtitle="Feat - ABH - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\nWhen an ally you can see within 60 feet of yourself expends XPHB, you can gain XPHB if you lack it. You can use this benefit a number of times equal to your XPHB, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB or XPHB."},
  ["feature.tireless-spirit.xge2024.fighter.samurai.10"]={title="Tireless Spirit",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 31\n\nStarting at 10th level, when you roll initiative and have no uses of Fighting Spirit remaining, you regain one use."},
  ["creature.tissina-khyret.wdh2014"]={title="Tissina Khyret",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 116\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 10 | WIS 13 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Infernal\n\nResistencias: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDark Devotion\n\nTissina has advantage on saving throws against being charmed or frightened.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nTissina makes two melee attacks.\n\nDagger\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage. Or Ranged Weapon Attack: 4 to hit, range 20/60 ft., one creature. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.titanothere.bgg2014"]={title="Titanothere",subtitle="Criatura - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 185\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / H\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 136 (13d12 + 52)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 10 | CON 19 | INT 2 | WIS 12 | CHA 6\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBeast of Burden\n\nThe titanothere is considered to be one size larger for the purpose of determining its carrying capacity.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nStomp\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h20 (3d8 + 7) bludgeoning damage. If the titanothere moved at least 20 feet straight toward the target immediately before the hit, the target takes an extra 13 (3d8) bludgeoning damage, and the target must succeed on a 18 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition if it is a creature."},
  ["creature.titivilus.mpmm2014"]={title="Titivilus",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 242\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 16\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 150 (20d8 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 60\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 22 | CON 17 | INT 24 | WIS 22 | CHA 26\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Titivilus fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nTitivilus has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nRegeneration\n\nTitivilus regains 10 hit points at the start of his turn. If he takes cold or radiant damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of his next turn. Titivilus dies only if he starts his turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\nVentriloquism\n\nWhenever Titivilus speaks, he can choose a point within 60 feet of him; his voice emanates from that point.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nTitivilus makes one Silver Sword attack, and he uses Frightful Word.\n\nSilver Sword\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) force damage, or 9 (1d10 + 4) force damage if used with two hands, plus 16 (3d10) necrotic damage. If the target is a creature, its hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to half the necrotic damage taken.\n\nFrightful Word\n\nTitivilus targets one creature he can see within 10 feet of him. The target must succeed on a 21 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened of him for 1 minute. While frightened in this way, the target must take the Dash action and move away from Titivilus by the safest available route on each of its turns, unless there is nowhere to move, in which case it needn't take the Dash action. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nTeleport\n\nTitivilus teleports, along with any equipment he is wearing or carrying, up to 120 feet to an unoccupied space he can see.\n\nTwisting Words\n\nTitivilus targets one creature he can see within 60 feet of him. The target must succeed on a 21 Charisma saving throw or become charmed by Titivilus for 1 minute. The charmed target can repeat the saving throw if Titivilus deals any damage to it. A creature that succeeds on the saving throw is immune to Titivilus's Twisting Words for 24 hours.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nCorrupting Guidance\n\nTitivilus uses Twisting Words. Alternatively, he targets one creature charmed by him that is within 60 feet of him; that charmed target must succeed on a 21 Charisma saving throw, or Titivilus decides how the target acts during its next turn.\n\nTeleport\n\nTitivilus uses Teleport.\n\nAssault (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nTitivilus makes one Silver Sword attack, or he uses Frightful Word."},
  ["creature.titivilus.mtf2014"]={title="Titivilus",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 179\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 16\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 127 (17d8 + 51)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 60\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 22 | CON 17 | INT 24 | WIS 22 | CHA 26\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Titivilus fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nTitivilus has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nTitivilus's weapon attacks are magical.\n\nRegeneration\n\nTitivilus regains 10 hit points at the start of his turn. If he takes cold or radiant damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of his next turn. Titivilus dies only if he starts his turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\nVentriloquism\n\nWhenever Titivilus speaks, he can choose a point within 60 feet; his voice emanates from that point.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nTitivilus makes one sword attack and uses his Frightful Word once.\n\nSilver Sword\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) slashing damage plus 16 (3d10) necrotic damage, or 9 (1d10 + 4) slashing damage plus 16 (3d10) necrotic damage if used with two hands. If the target is a creature, its hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to half the necrotic damage it takes.\n\nFrightful Word\n\nTitivilus targets one creature he can see within 10 feet of him. The target must succeed on a 21 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. While frightened in this way, the target must take the Dash action and move away from Titivilus by the safest available route on each of its turns, unless there is nowhere to move, in which case it needn't take the Dash action. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nTeleport\n\nTitivilus magically teleports, along with any equipment he is wearing and carrying, up to 120 feet to an unoccupied space he can see.\n\nTwisting Words\n\nTitivilus targets one creature he can see within 60 feet of him. The target must make a 21 Charisma saving throw. On a failure the target is charmed for 1 minute. The charmed target can repeat the saving throw if Titivilus deals any damage to it. A creature that succeeds on the saving throw is immune to Titivilus's Twisting Words for 24 hours.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nAssault (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nTitivilus attacks with his silver sword or uses his Frightful Word.\n\nCorrupting Guidance\n\nTitivilus uses Twisting Words. Alternatively, he targets one creature charmed by him that is within 60 feet of him; that charmed target must make a 21 Charisma saving throw. On a failure, Titivilus decides how the target acts during its next turn.\n\nTeleport\n\nTitivilus uses his Teleport action."},
  ["creature.tixie-tockworth.kftgv2014"]={title="Tixie Tockworth",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 85\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 75 (10d6 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 13 | CON 18 | INT 17 | WIS 9 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Gnomish, Terran, Undercommon\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nForce Field\n\nTockworth generates a magical force field around herself. This force field has 15 hit points and regains all its hit points at the start of each of Tockworth's turns, but it ceases to function if Tockworth drops to 0 hit points. Any damage Tockworth takes is subtracted from the force field's hit points first. Each time the force field regains hit points, the following conditions end on Tockworth: grappled, restrained, and stunned.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nTockworth makes three Shortsword or Lightning Discharge attacks.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) force damage.\n\nLightning Discharge\n\nrs 6 to hit, range 60 ft., one creature. h16 (3d10) lightning damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nScalding Steam {@recharge 5}\n\nTockworth emits a jet of piping-hot steam in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in that cone must make a 15 Dexterity saving throw, taking 10 (3d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.tixie-s-shield-guardian.kftgv2014"]={title="Tixie's Shield Guardian",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 80\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.tlacatecolo.jttrc2014"]={title="Tlacatecolo",subtitle="Criatura - JttRC - 2014",body="Pagina: 65\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 78 (12d8 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 17 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 15 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common\n\nResistencias: cold, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe tlacatecolo has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe tlacatecolo makes two Talon attacks.\n\nTalon\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage plus 14 (3d8) poison damage.\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe tlacatecolo magically transforms into a Medium owl, while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation ends if the tlacatecolo is reduced to 0 hit points or if it uses its action to end it.\n\nPlague Winds (Fiend Form Only; Recharge 5-6)\n\nThe tlacatecolo emits a chilling, disease-ridden wind in a 60-foot line that is 10 feet wide. Each creature in that area must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or take 26 (4d12) cold damage and become poisoned.\n\nWhile poisoned in this way, the creature can't regain hit points. At the end of every hour, the creature must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or gain 1 level of exhaustion. If the creature is in direct sunlight when it makes this saving throw, it automatically succeeds on the save.\n\nIf the creature is targeted by magic that ends a poison or disease, such as lesser restoration, while the creature isn't in direct sunlight, the effect does not end."},
  ["creature.tlexolotl.jttrc2014"]={title="Tlexolotl",subtitle="Criatura - JttRC - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / H\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 104 (11d12 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 10 | CON 17 | INT 7 | WIS 13 | CHA 9\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft., tremorsense 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Ignan\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFire Aura\n\nAt the start of each of the tlexolotl's turns, each creature within 10 feet of it takes 7 (2d6) fire damage, and flammable objects in that aura that aren't being worn or carried ignite. A creature that touches the tlexolotl or hits it with a melee attack while within 5 feet of it takes 7 (2d6) fire damage.\n\nIllumination\n\nThe tlexolotl sheds bright light in a 30-foot radius and dim light for an additional 30 feet.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe tlexolotl regains 10 hit points at the start of its turn. If the tlexolotl takes cold damage or is immersed in water, this trait doesn't function at the start of the tlexolotl's next turn. The tlexolotl dies only if it starts its turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe tlexolotl makes one Bite attack and one Tail attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h12 (1d10 + 7) piercing damage plus 18 (4d8) fire damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h11 (1d8 + 7) bludgeoning damage plus 14 (4d6) fire damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 19 Strength saving throw or be pushed up to 10 feet away from the tlexolotl and knocked prone.\n\nPyroclasm {@recharge 5}\n\nGouts of molten lava erupt from the tlexolotl's body. Each creature in a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on the tlexolotl must make a 15 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed saving throw, a creature takes 21 (6d6) fire damage and 21 (6d6) bludgeoning damage. On a successful saving throw, a creature takes half as much damage."},
  ["creature.tlincalli.mpmm2014"]={title="Tlincalli",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 242\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 85 (10d10 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 13 | CON 16 | INT 8 | WIS 12 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Tlincalli\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe tlincalli makes one Longsword or Spiked Chain attack and one Sting attack.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) slashing damage, or 8 (1d10 + 3) slashing damage if used with two hands.\n\nSpiked Chain\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage, and the target is grappled (escape 11) if it is a Large or smaller creature. Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained, and the tlincalli can't use the spiked chain against another target.\n\nSting\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage plus 14 (4d6) poison damage, and the target must succeed on a 14 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned for 1 minute. If it fails the saving throw by 5 or more, the target is also paralyzed while poisoned. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.tlincalli.vgm2014"]={title="Tlincalli",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 193\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 85 (10d10 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 13 | CON 16 | INT 8 | WIS 12 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Tlincalli\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe tlincalli makes two attacks: one with its longsword or spiked chain, and one with its sting.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) slashing damage, or 8 (1d10 + 3) slashing damage if used with two hands.\n\nSpiked Chain\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage, and the target is grappled (escape 11) if it is a Large or smaller creature. Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained, and the tlincalli can't use the spiked chain against another target.\n\nSting\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage plus 14 (4d6) poison damage, and the target must succeed on a 14 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned for 1 minute. If it fails the saving throw by 5 or more, the target is also paralyzed while poisoned. The target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["language.tlincalli.vgm2014"]={title="Tlincalli",subtitle="Idioma - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 193"},
  ["magicitem.tloques-berserker-battleaxe.tftyp2014"]={title="Tloques' Berserker Battleaxe",subtitle="Item Magico - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 68\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis battleaxe has a blade of bronze, and the haft is wound with snakeskin wrappings. It casts an ominous shadow in the shape of what appears to be a withered arm. Those within reach of it feel a cold chill run up and down their spine.\n\nConcealed beneath the wrappings around the handle is a parchment containing the spells passwall, burning hands, and gust of wind. When the attuned wielder uses an action to say the correct words of power, which are engraved in Olman on the axe blade, one of these spells can be cast.\n\nThe axe has 12 charges and regains 1d6 + 4 expended charges daily at dawn. Casting a spell from it takes a number of charges equal to the level at which the spell is cast (5th for passwall, 2nd for gust of wind, and 1st or higher for burning hands; spell save 15). If the parchment is removed from the axe, the axe loses the capability of casting these spells forever.\n\nYou gain a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. In addition, while you are attuned to this weapon, your hit point maximum increases by 1 for each level you have attained.\n\nCurse\n\nThis axe is cursed, and becoming attuned to it extends the curse to you. As long as you remain cursed, you are unwilling to part with the axe, keeping it within reach at all times. You also have disadvantage on attack rolls with weapons other than this one, unless no foe is within 60 feet of you that you can see or hear.\n\nWhenever a hostile creature damages you while the axe is in your possession, you must succeed on a 15 Wisdom saving throw or go berserk. While berserk, you must use your action each round to attack the creature nearest to you with the axe. If you can make extra attacks as part of the Attack action, you use those extra attacks, moving to attack the next nearest creature after you fell your current target. If you have multiple possible targets, you attack one at random. You are berserk until you start your turn with no creatures within 60 feet of you that you can see or hear."},
  ["creature.tloques-popolocas.tftyp2014"]={title="Tloques-Popolocas",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 68\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 82 (11d8 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 16 | CON 16 | INT 11 | WIS 10 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: the languages it knew in life\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe vampire regains 10 hit points at the start of its turn if it has at least 1 hit point and isn't in sunlight or running water. If the vampire takes radiant damage or damage from PHB, this trait doesn't function at the start of the vampire's next turn.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe vampire can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nVampire Weaknesses\n\nThe vampire has the following flaws:\n\n• Forbiddance\n\n• Harmed by Running Water\n\n• Stake to the Heart\n\n• Sunlight Hypersensitivity\n\nShapechanger\n\nIf the vampire isn't in sunlight or running water, it can use its action to Polymorph into a Tiny bat, or back into its true form.\n\nWhile in bat form, the vampire can't speak, its walking speed is 5 feet, and it has a flying speed of 30 feet. Its Statistics, other than its size and speed, are unchanged. Anything it is wearing transforms with it, but nothing it is carrying does. It reverts to its true form if it dies.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe vampire makes two attacks.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h8 (2d4 + 3) slashing damage. Instead of dealing damage, the vampire can grapple the target, escape 13.\n\nChildren of the Night (1/Day)\n\nThe vampire magically calls 2d4 swarms of bats, provided that the sun isn't up. The called creatures arrive in 1d4 rounds, acting as allies of the vampire and obeying its spoken commands. The beasts remain for 1 hour, until the vampire dies, or until the vampire dismisses them as a bonus action.\n\nTloques' Berserker Axe +2\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d8 + 5) slashing damage."},
  ["item.tocken.scag2014"]={title="Tocken",subtitle="Item - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 124\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA hanging set of carved oval bells, usually played with a pair of light wooden hammers (or open handed). They are most common in underground cultures, where the resonant tones can carry."},
  ["feature.tokens-of-the-departed.rhw2014.rogue.phantom.9"]={title="Tokens of the Departed",subtitle="Caracteristica - RHW - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.tokens-of-the-departed.tce2014.rogue.phantom.9"]={title="Tokens of the Departed",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 62\n\n9th-level Phantom feature\n\nWhen a life ends in your presence, you're able to snatch a token from the departing soul, a sliver of its life essence that takes physical form: as a reaction when a creature you can see dies within 30 feet of you, you can open your free hand and cause a Tiny trinket to appear there, a soul trinket. The DM determines the trinket's form or has you roll on the phb table in the Player's Handbook to generate it. You can have a maximum number of soul trinkets equal to your proficiency bonus, and you can't create one while at your maximum.\n\nYou can use soul trinkets in the following ways:\n\n• While a soul trinket is on your person, you have advantage on death saving throws and Constitution saving throws, for your vitality is enhanced by the life essence within the object.\n\n• When you deal Sneak Attack damage on your turn, you can destroy one of your soul trinkets that's on your person and then immediately use Wails from the Grave, without expending a use of that feature.\n\n• As an action, you can destroy one of your soul trinkets, no matter where it's located. When you do so, you can ask the spirit associated with the trinket one question. The spirit appears to you and answers in a language it knew in life. It's under no obligation to be truthful, and it answers as concisely as possible, eager to be free. The spirit knows only what it knew in life, as determined by the DM."},
  ["spell.toll-the-dead.xge2024"]={title="Toll the Dead",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 169\n\nYou point at one creature you can see within range, and the sound of a dolorous bell fills the air around it for a moment. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or take 1d8 necrotic damage. If the target is missing any of its hit points, it instead takes 1d12 necrotic damage.\n\nThe spell's damage increases by one die when you reach 5th level (2d8 or 2d12), 11th level (3d8 or 3d12), and 17th level (4d8 or 4d12)."},
  ["spell.toll-the-dead.xphb2024"]={title="Toll the Dead",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 334\n\nYou point at one creature you can see within range, and the single chime of a dolorous bell is audible within 10 feet of the target. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or take 1d8 Necrotic damage. If the target is missing any of its XPHB, it instead takes 1d12 Necrotic damage."},
  ["creature.tomb-dwarf.toa2014"]={title="Tomb Dwarf",subtitle="Criatura - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 135\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 45 (6d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 10 | WIS 13 | CHA 15\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: the languages it knew in life\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, the tomb dwarf has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe tomb dwarf makes two longsword attacks or two crossbow attacks. It can use its Life Drain in place of one longsword attack.\n\nLife Drain\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h5 (1d6 + 2) necrotic damage. The target must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or its hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to the damage taken. This reduction lasts until the target finishes a long rest. The target dies if this effect reduces its hit point maximum to 0.A humanoid slain by this attack rises 24 hours later as a zombie under the tomb dwarf's control, unless the humanoid is restored to life or its body is destroyed. The tomb dwarf can have no more than twelve zombies under its control at one time.\n\nBattleaxe\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) slashing damage, or 7 (1d10 + 2) slashing damage if used with two hands.\n\nLight Crossbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.tomb-guardian.toa2014"]={title="Tomb Guardian",subtitle="Criatura - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 127\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 93 (11d8 + 44)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 9 | CON 18 | INT 6 | WIS 10 | CHA 5\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages of its creator but can't speak\n\nImunidades: lightning, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBerserk\n\nWhenever the tomb guardian starts its turn with 40 hit points or fewer, roll a d6. On a 6, the tomb guardian goes berserk. On each of its turns while berserk, the tomb guardian attacks the nearest creature it can see. If no creature is near enough to move to and attack, the tomb guardian attacks an object, with preference for an object smaller than itself. Once the tomb guardian goes berserk, it continues to do so until it is destroyed or regains all its hit points. The golem's creator, if within 60 feet of the berserk tomb guardian, can try to calm it by speaking firmly and persuasively. The tomb guardian must be able to hear its creator, who must take an action to make a 15 Charisma (Persuasion) check. If the check succeeds, the tomb guardian ceases being berserk. If it takes damage while still at 40 hit points or fewer, the tomb guardian might go berserk again.\n\nAversion of Fire\n\nIf the tomb guardian takes fire damage, it has disadvantage on attack rolls and ability checks until the end of its next turn.\n\nImmutable Form\n\nThe tomb guardian is immune to any spell or effect that would alter its form.\n\nLightning Absorption\n\nWhenever the tomb guardian is subjected to lightning damage, it takes no damage and instead regains a number of hit points equal to the lightning damage dealt.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe tomb guardian has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe golem's weapon attacks are magical.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe tomb guardian makes two slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["optionalfeature.tomb-of-levistus.xge2024"]={title="Tomb of Levistus",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 57\n\nAs a reaction when you take damage, you can entomb yourself in ice, which melts away at the end of your next turn. You gain 10 temporary hit points per warlock level, which take as much of the triggering damage as possible. Immediately after you take the damage, you gain vulnerability to fire damage, your speed is reduced to 0, and you are incapacitated. These effects, including any remaining temporary hit points, all end when the ice melts.\n\nOnce you use this invocation, you can't use it again until you finish a short or long rest."},
  ["creature.tomb-tapper.idrotf2014"]={title="Tomb Tapper",subtitle="Criatura - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 310\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / H\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 207 (18d12 + 90)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 10\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 10 | CON 21 | INT 14 | WIS 14 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 240 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nIdiomas: understands Common and Undercommon but doesn't speak, telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: lightning\n\nImunidades: cold, fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPetrified Death\n\nA tomb tapper reduced to 0 hit points turns into a lifeless stone statue. Anything it's wearing or carrying is not transformed.\n\nSense Magic\n\nThe tomb tapper senses magic within 30 feet of it and can use an action to pinpoint the location of any creature, object, or area in that range that bears magic. This sense penetrates barriers but is blocked by a thin sheet of lead.\n\nTunneler\n\nThe tomb tapper can burrow through solid rock at half its burrowing speed and leaves a 10-foot-wide, 20-foot-tall tunnel in its wake.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe tomb tapper doesn't require air or sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe tomb tapper makes two melee attacks with its sledgehammer or with its claws. If it hits the same creature with both claws, it can pull that creature within 5 feet of its mouth and make a bite attack against it.\n\nBite\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h22 (3d10 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (3d6 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nSledgehammer\n\nmw,rw 10 to hit, reach 15 ft. or range 30/120 ft., one target. h27 (6d6 + 6) bludgeoning or force damage (tomb tapper's choice). If thrown, the hammer returns to the tomb tapper at the end of its turn, landing at the tomb tapper's feet if it doesn't have a hand free to catch the weapon."},
  ["magicitem.tome-of-clear-thought.dmg2014"]={title="Tome of Clear Thought",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 208\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis book contains memory and logic exercises, and its words are charged with magic. If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book's contents and practicing its guidelines, your Intelligence score increases by 2, as does your maximum for that score. The manual then loses its magic, but regains it in a century."},
  ["magicitem.tome-of-clear-thought.xdmg2024"]={title="Tome of Clear Thought",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 317\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis book contains memory and logic exercises, and its words are charged with magic. If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book's contents and practicing its guidelines, your Intelligence increases by 2, to a maximum of 30. The manual then loses its magic, but regains it in a century."},
  ["magicitem.tome-of-leadership-and-influence.dmg2014"]={title="Tome of Leadership and Influence",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 208\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis book contains guidelines for influencing and charming others, and its words are charged with magic. If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book's contents and practicing its guidelines, your Charisma score increases by 2, as does your maximum for that score. The manual then loses its magic, but regains it in a century."},
  ["magicitem.tome-of-leadership-and-influence.xdmg2024"]={title="Tome of Leadership and Influence",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 317\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis book contains guidelines for influencing and charming others, and its words are charged with magic. If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book's contents and practicing its guidelines, your Charisma increases by 2, to a maximum of 30. The manual then loses its magic, but regains it in a century."},
  ["item.tome-of-strahd.cos2014"]={title="Tome of Strahd",subtitle="Item - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 221\n\nRaridade: none\n\nThe Tome of Strahd is an ancient work penned by Strahd, a tragic tale of how he came to his fallen state. The book is bound in a thick leather cover with steel hinges and fastenings. The pages are of parchment and very brittle. Most of the book is written in the curious shorthand that only Strahd employs. Stains and age have made most of the work illegible, but several paragraphs remain intact."},
  ["magicitem.tome-of-the-dragon.fraif2014"]={title="Tome of the Dragon",subtitle="Item Magico - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 247\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nThis heavy tome is bound in dragonhide and reinforced with thick bands of cold iron. The original copies were made by wyrmspeakers of the FRHoF and bear that cult's symbol on their cover. The Tome of the Dragon contains the secret ritual to transform a dragon or a dead dragon's body into a dracolich.\n\nTo decipher and use the Tome of the Dragon, you must be either a spellcaster with at least two level 5 spell slots or a Dragon. A single assistant (or more, at the DM's discretion) can help you conduct the ritual, so long as that assistant also meets the requirements to use the tome.\n\nTo create a dracolich using a Tome of the Dragon, you must have continuous access to the body of an adult or ancient dragon (either living or dead), as well as 80,000 GP worth of supplies (which includes a gem that will serve as the anchor for the dracolich's spirit). While you have the necessary materials, you must conduct a ritual that lasts 180 days divided by the number of creatures conducting the ritual. During the ritual, you and any assistants must work without interruption, resting no more than 8 hours per day. If you are a Dragon, the cost of supplies and the ritual's duration are halved.\n\nWhen the ritual is complete, the tome explodes with violet light, dealing (12d6) Necrotic damage to you and each assistant. If this damage reduces a creature to 0 XPHB, the creature is killed and immediately reanimates as a XMM under the DM's control.\n\nAt the end of the ritual, the target transforms into a XMM. If the ritual's target was a living dragon, that dragon dies instantly, and its spirit is transferred to the gem supplied for the ritual. If the target was a dead dragon's body, the body reanimates, and the gem is inhabited by an evil dragon spirit from the Outer Planes. The dracolich is under no obligation toward its creators and acts according to its nature."},
  ["magicitem.tome-of-the-stilled-tongue.dmg2014"]={title="Tome of the Stilled Tongue",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 208\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nThis thick leather-bound volume has a desiccated tongue pinned to the front cover. Five of these tomes exist, and it's unknown which one is the original. The grisly cover decoration on the first tome of the stilled tongue once belonged to a treacherous former servant of the lich-god Vecna, keeper of secrets. The tongues pinned to the covers of the four copies came from other spellcasters who crossed Vecna. The first few pages of each tome are filled with indecipherable scrawls. The remaining pages are blank and pristine.\n\nIf you can attune to this item, you can use it as a spellbook and an arcane focus. In addition, while holding the tome, you can use a bonus action to cast a spell you have written in this tome, without expending a spell slot or using any verbal or somatic component. Once used, this property of the tome can't be used again until the next dawn.\n\nWhile attuned to the book, you can remove the tongue from the book's cover. If you do so, all spells written in the book are permanently erased.\n\nVecna watches anyone using this tome. He can also write cryptic messages in the book. These messages appear at midnight and fade away after they are read."},
  ["magicitem.tome-of-the-stilled-tongue.xdmg2024"]={title="Tome of the Stilled Tongue",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 317\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nThis book has a desiccated tongue pinned to its front cover. Five of these tomes exist, and it's unknown which one is the original. The tongue on the first Tome of the Stilled Tongue belonged to a treacherous former servant of the lich XDMG. The tongues pinned to the covers of the four copies came from other spellcasters who crossed Vecna. The first few pages of each tome are filled with indecipherable scrawls. The remaining pages are blank.\n\nWhile attuned to this item, you can use it as a Spellbook and an Arcane Focus. In addition, while holding the tome, you can take a XPHB to cast a spell you have written in this tome, without expending a spell slot or using any Verbal or Somatic components. Once used, this property of the tome can't be used again until the next dawn.\n\nOnly you can remove the tongue from the book's cover. If you do so, all spells written in the book are permanently erased.\n\nVecna watches anyone using this tome and can write cryptic messages in it. These messages typically fade away after they are read."},
  ["magicitem.tome-of-understanding.dmg2014"]={title="Tome of Understanding",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 209\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis book contains intuition and insight exercises, and its words are charged with magic. If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book's contents and practicing its guidelines, your Wisdom score increases by 2, as does your maximum for that score. The manual then loses its magic, but regains it in a century."},
  ["magicitem.tome-of-understanding.xdmg2024"]={title="Tome of Understanding",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 317\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis book contains intuition and insight exercises, and its words are charged with magic. If you spend 48 hours over a period of 6 days or fewer studying the book's contents and practicing its guidelines, your Wisdom increases by 2, to a maximum of 30. The manual then loses its magic, but regains it in a century."},
  ["creature.tommy-two-butts.rmbre2014"]={title="Tommy Two-Butts",subtitle="Criatura - RMBRE - 2014",body="Pagina: 18\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nINT 21"},
  ["creature.tonalli.jttrc2014"]={title="Tonalli",subtitle="Criatura - JttRC - 2014",body="Pagina: 110\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["reward.tongue-of-the-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Tongue of the Dragon",subtitle="Recompensa - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 28\n\nYou gain some of the majestic presence of a dragon.\n\nDragon's Speech\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Draconic.\n\nDragon's Voice\n\nAs a bonus action, you can make your voice audible up to 300 feet away for 1 minute.\n\nDragon's Wiles\n\nYou have advantage on Charisma (Persuasion) checks."},
  ["feature.tongue-of-the-sun-and-moon.phb2014.monk.base.13"]={title="Tongue of the Sun and Moon",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 76\n\nStarting at 13th level, you learn to touch the ki of other minds so that you understand all spoken languages. Moreover, any creature that can understand a language can understand what you say."},
  ["spell.tongues.phb2014"]={title="Tongues",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 283\n\nThis spell grants the creature you touch the ability to understand any spoken language it hears. Moreover, when the target speaks, any creature that knows at least one language and can hear the target understands what it says."},
  ["spell.tongues.xphb2024"]={title="Tongues",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 334\n\nThis spell grants the creature you touch the ability to understand any spoken or signed language that it hears or sees. Moreover, when the target communicates by speaking or signing, any creature that knows at least one language can understand it if that creature can hear the speech or see the signing."},
  ["feature.tool-expertise.tce2014.artificer.base.6"]={title="Tool Expertise",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\n6th-level artificer feature\n\nYour proficiency bonus is now doubled for any ability check you make that uses your proficiency with a tool."},
  ["feature.tool-proficiency.tce2014.artificer.alchemist.3"]={title="Tool Proficiency",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.tool-proficiency.tce2014.artificer.artillerist.3"]={title="Tool Proficiency",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.tool-proficiency.tce2014.artificer.battle-smith.3"]={title="Tool Proficiency",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.tools-of-the-trade.efa2014.artificer.alchemist.3"]={title="Tools of the Trade",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.tools-of-the-trade.efa2014.artificer.armorer.3"]={title="Tools of the Trade",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.tools-of-the-trade.efa2014.artificer.artillerist.3"]={title="Tools of the Trade",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.tools-of-the-trade.efa2014.artificer.battle-smith.3"]={title="Tools of the Trade",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.tools-of-the-trade.efa2014.artificer.cartographer.3"]={title="Tools of the Trade",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.tools-of-the-trade.tce2014.artificer.armorer.3"]={title="Tools of the Trade",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["creature.tooth-n-claw.slw2014"]={title="Tooth-N-Claw",subtitle="Criatura - SLW - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 45 (7d8 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 12 | CON 14 | INT 6 | WIS 13 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Infernal but can't speak it\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Hearing and Smell\n\nTooth-N-Claw has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or smell.\n\nPack Tactics\n\nTooth-N-Claw has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of its allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) cold damage.\n\nFreezing Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nTooth-N-Claw exhales an icy blast in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 12 Dexterity saving throw, taking 21 (6d6) cold damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["item.topaz.dmg2014"]={title="Topaz",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA transparent golden yellow gemstone."},
  ["item.topaz.xdmg2024"]={title="Topaz",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA golden yellow gemstone."},
  ["magicitem.topaz-annihilator.ftd2014"]={title="Topaz Annihilator",subtitle="Item Magico - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nThis magic ranged weapon resembles a DMG, but in lieu of any ammunition, it holds a glowing yellow scale from a topaz dragon in its heart.\n\nThe weapon has a normal range of 100 feet and a long range of 300 feet, and it has the two-handed property. It deals 2d6 necrotic damage on a hit. If this damage reduces a creature or object to 0 hit points, the target is reduced to dust. A creature reduced to dust can be restored to life only by a true resurrection or wish spell.\n\nWhile the weapon is on your person, you can use an action to cast the disintegrate spell (save 18). Once this property is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["creature.topaz-dragon-wyrmling.ftd2014"]={title="Topaz Dragon Wyrmling",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 223\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60, swim: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 12 | CON 13 | INT 14 | WIS 13 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 10 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nResistencias: cold, necrotic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe both air and water.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) piercing damage plus 2 (1d4) necrotic damage.\n\nDesiccating Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales yellowish necrotic energy in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 11 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 21 (6d6) necrotic damage and is weakened until the end of its next turn. A weakened creature has disadvantage on Strength-based ability checks and Strength saving throws, and the creature's weapon attacks that rely on Strength deal half damage. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't weakened."},
  ["creature.topaz-greatwyrm.ftd2014"]={title="Topaz Greatwyrm",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 201\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 26\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 507 (26d20 + 234)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, burrow: 60, fly: 120, swim: 60\n\nSTR 28 | DEX 14 | CON 29 | INT 30 | WIS 24 | CHA 25\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: necrotic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nGem Awakening (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nIf the greatwyrm would be reduced to 0 hit points, its current hit point total instead resets to 400 hit points, it recharges its Breath Weapon, and it regains any expended uses of Legendary Resistance. Additionally, the greatwyrm can now use its Mass Telekinesis action during the next hour. Award a party an additional 90,000 XP (180,000 XP total) for defeating the greatwyrm after its Gem Awakening activates.\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day)\n\nIf the greatwyrm fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe greatwyrm doesn't require food or drink.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe greatwyrm makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h20 (2d10 + 9) piercing damage plus 16 (3d10) force damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h18 (2d8 + 9) slashing damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it is grappled (escape 19) and is restrained until this grapple ends. The greatwyrm can have only one creature grappled in this way at a time.\n\nBreath Weapon {@recharge 5}\n\nThe greatwyrm exhales crushing force in a 300-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 25 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 71 (11d12) force damage and is knocked prone. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage and isn't knocked prone. On a success or failure, the creature's speed becomes 0 until the end of its next turn.\n\nMass Telekinesis (Gem Awakening Only; Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe greatwyrm targets any number of creatures and objects it can see within 120 feet of it. No one target can weigh more than 4,000 pounds, and objects can't be targeted if they're being worn or carried. Each targeted creature must succeed on a 26 Strength saving throw or be restrained in the greatwyrm's telekinetic grip. At the end of a creature's turn, it can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nAt the end of the greatwyrm's turn, it can move each creature or object it has in its telekinetic grip up to 60 feet in any direction, but not beyond 120 feet of itself. In addition, it can choose any number of creatures restrained in this way and deal 45 (7d12) force damage to each of them.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe greatwyrm magically transforms into any creature that is Medium or Small, while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation ends if the greatwyrm is reduced to 0 hit points or uses a bonus action to end it.\n\nPsychic Step\n\nThe greatwyrm magically teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 60 feet of it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nThe greatwyrm makes one Claw attack.\n\nPsionics (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe greatwyrm uses Psychic Step or Spellcasting.\n\nPsychic Beam (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe greatwyrm emits a beam of psychic energy in a 90-foot line that is 10 feet wide. Each creature in that area must make a 26 Intelligence saving throw, taking 27 (5d10) psychic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.topi.ttp2014"]={title="Topi",subtitle="Criatura - TTP - 2014",body="Pagina: 22\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / S\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 13 (3d6 + 3)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 7 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 6 | WIS 10 | CHA 5\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages it knew in life but can't speak\n\nResistencias: bludgeoning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nTurn Resistance\n\nThe topi has advantage on saving throws against any effect that turns undead.\n\nUndead Fortitude\n\nIf damage reduces the topi to 0 hit points, it must make a Constitution saving throw with a DC of 5+the damage taken, unless the damage is radiant or from a critical hit. On a success, the topi drops to 1 hit point instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nVenomous Claws\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) slashing damage plus 2 (1d4) poison damage, and the target must succeed on a 11 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned until the end of the target's next turn."},
  ["creature.topolah.lox2014"]={title="Topolah",subtitle="Criatura - LoX - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.topsy.oota2014"]={title="Topsy",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nIdiomas: Gnomish, Terran, Undercommon"},
