  ["item.torch.phb2014"]={title="Torch",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 153\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA torch burns for 1 hour, providing bright light in a 20-foot radius and dim light for an additional 20 feet. If you make a melee attack with a burning torch and hit, it deals 1 fire damage."},
  ["item.torch.xphb2024"]={title="Torch",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 229\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA Torch burns for 1 hour, casting XPHB in a 20-foot radius and XPHB for an additional 20 feet. When you take the XPHB action, you can attack with the Torch, using it as a Simple Melee weapon. On a hit, the target takes 1 Fire damage."},
  ["creature.torgja-stonecrusher-levels-1-4.kftgv2014"]={title="Torgja Stonecrusher (Levels 1-4)",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.torgja-stonecrusher-levels-5-8.kftgv2014"]={title="Torgja Stonecrusher (Levels 5-8)",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.torgja-stonecrusher-levels-9-11.kftgv2014"]={title="Torgja Stonecrusher (Levels 9-11)",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.torlin-silvershield.tftyp2014"]={title="Torlin Silvershield",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 159\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["deity.torm.frhof2014"]={title="Torm",subtitle="Divindade - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 125\n\nThose who favor Torm believe salvation is found through service. He is a god of courage and self-sacrifice, an unyielding deity who dutifully puts himself on the front line of the fight against evil and injustice. He is a patron god of many Paladins, embodying the tenets of the Oath of Devotion.\n\nTorm's name carries gravitas and strikes fear into treacherous hearts, but his heart is filled with goodness. In legends, he is kind and gentle when dealing with faithful friends, the weak, and the defenseless. But he is stern and righteous against the forces of evil and injustice. When Torm appears in dreams, he takes the form of an enormous, flying metal gauntlet surrounded by arcs of lightning. He might send a golden XMM or, in extreme cases, a XMM clad in gleaming armor to make his will known.\n\nTorm's faithful believe that brave acts of service please their god. They strive to maintain peace and order while opposing unjust laws and standing alert against corruption. Though many of Torm's followers are warriors, skill in combat isn't required to uphold Torm's ideals. For instance, a council member who worships Torm advocates for what is just, even if this puts their position at risk. Torm's followers believe every failure of duty diminishes Torm and every success adds to his luster. The faithful know everyone stumbles from time to time, but they never cease aspiring to Torm's standards.\n\nFollowers construct fortress-temples dedicated to Torm on defensible heights. These structures offer drilling grounds, stables, and austere quarters for residents and visiting knights. Lion statues and armored figures feature in these temples' decor, with the coats of arms of fallen heroes decorating the white-granite walls. The priesthood of Torm is friendly with the priesthoods of Tyr and Ilmater: together with Torm, these gods make up a trio of deities called the Triad. Torm's priests are also allied with the Red Knight and Lathander.\n\nChosen of Torm dedicate themselves to the fight against evil, especially against the forces of Bane. Torm and Bane battled each other to their mutual destruction during the Time of Troubles—both gods have since returned, and the animosity between them still seethes.\n\nOrder of the Golden Lion\n\nEast of the FRHoF, the city of Tantras is home to the greatest concentration of Torm worshipers in Faerûn. There, Torm manifested and slew Bane during the Time of Troubles. While this era was a time of great pride for Torm's followers, it also became one of great shame. After returning to his godly state, Torm was disgusted to find that Tantras's priests had been persecuting believers of other gods, and that this practice had spread throughout the Dalelands and along the Sea of Fallen Stars. As punishment, Torm dictated a series of responsibilities and obligations—the Penance of Duty—for his followers to perform as atonement. Over a century has passed since this decree, and Torm's followers have regained trust in the regions around Tantras. Still, a select group of Torm's faithful vowed to continue the atonement of the Penance of Duty, and those people are known as the Order of the Golden Lion.\n\nThe Order of the Golden Lion involves righting three Debts: Persecution, Dereliction, and Destruction. Typically knights of the Golden Lion devote themselves to righting a single debt. Those who choose the Debt of Persecution aid good religions wherever possible. Followers of the Debt of Dereliction atone for abdications of duty by seeking out and eliminating cults of Bane, as well as routing the FRHoF. Adherents to the Debt of Destruction are obliged to report and repair areas of dead magic and wild magic throughout Faerûn as penance for the destruction to FRHoF caused by Torm's battle against Bane.\n\nThe Order of the Golden Lion is most active in the Dalelands and the region around Tantras, but faithful as far as the FRHoF have picked up the mantle. The order is largely composed of warriors, and members wear the order's signature article of clothing: a pair of golden pauldrons, each carved in the shape of a lion's head. To become a member of the Order of the Golden Lion, an individual must prove their dedication by completing a holy quest for a temple of Torm. (If your campaign uses renown, a character must also have a Renown Score of 5+ with the Order of the Golden Lion to join the organization.)"},
  ["deity.torm.phb2014"]={title="Torm",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 294"},
  ["deity.torm.scag2014"]={title="Torm",subtitle="Divindade - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\nTorm is the god of duty and loyalty, revered by those who face danger to bring about a greater good. Those who favor Torm believe that one's salvation can be found through service, that every failure to perform one's duty diminishes Torm, and that every success adds to his luster. Those who take Torm to heart must strive to fulfill his commandment to go out into the world and be an active force for good, to right wrongs, and to help the hopeless. They must strive to maintain peace and order while opposing unjust laws. Followers of Torm stand ever alert against corruption and are expected to strike quickly and hard against any evidence of rot in the hearts of mortals. As the sword arm of justice, Torm's faithful are expected to bring quick deaths to betrayers. Considering these tenets, it should be no surprise that most human paladins have Torm as their patron.\n\nMost temples dedicated to Torm are fortresses built on heights. These structures offer austere quarters for residents and visiting knights, drilling grounds, and stables. White granite, lion statues, and armored figures predominate in the architecture, with the coats of arms of fallen heroes decorating the walls of the great halls.\n\nTorm is seen as the good right hand of Tyr, and as such his symbol is a white gauntlet made for the right hand. It represents Tyr's sword hand, but it is also a symbol of forbearance. Torm is frequently depicted with his right gauntlet extended palm forward, which worshipers call the Hand Resolute. It signifies the principle that the just and true must pause before acting to judge whether their intentions uphold Torm's ideals. Temples, civic structures, and the homes of the faithful are often decorated with images of the Hand Resolute as a constant reminder of this principle.\n\nWorshipers of Torm come from most walks of life, for he welcomes any who seek the best in themselves and others, who uphold his tenets of loyalty, responsibility, duty, and kindness, or who are willing to sacrifice to keep evil from gaining ascendancy in the world. The faithful know that all of them will stumble from time to time while following in Torm's footsteps, but Torm's priests teach that the shame of a minor fall from grace is far less severe than declining to rise oneself up to Torm's standards."},
  ["vehicle.tormentor.bgdia2014"]={title="Tormentor",subtitle="Veiculo - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 218\n\nCrushing Wheels\n\nThe Tormentor can move through the space of any Medium or smaller creature. When it does, the creature must succeed on a 13 Dexterity saving throw or take 11 (2d10) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone.If the creature was already prone, it takes an extra 11 (2d10) bludgeoning damage.This trait can't be used against a particular creature more than once each turn.\n\nProne Deficiency\n\nIf the Tormentor rolls over and falls prone, it can't right itself and is incapacitated until flipped upright.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe Tormentor's weapon attacks are magical.\n\nRaking Scythes\n\nWhen the Tormentor moves within 5 feet of a creature that isn't prone or another vehicle for the first time on a turn, it can rake the creature or vehicle with its protruding blades for 13 (2d10 + 2) slashing damage. A creature moves out of the way and takes no damage if it succeeds on a 13 Dexterity saving throw.A vehicle moves out of the way and takes no damage if its driver succeeds on the saving throw.\n\nJuke\n\nIf the Tormentor is able to move, the driver can use its reaction to grant the Tormentor advantage on a Dexterity saving throw."},
  ["creature.tornscale.pota2014"]={title="Tornscale",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 90\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nPV: 36 (4d8 + 4)"},
  ["deity.torog.dmg2014"]={title="Torog",subtitle="Divindade - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 10"},
  ["deity.torog.egw2014"]={title="Torog",subtitle="Divindade - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 28\n\nThe dark god of the endless tunnels and caverns beneath Exandria, Torog is the patron of torturers, slavers, and jailers across the realms. His violent tears carved the pathways under the world, and his realm of imprisonment is a network of deadly caves and manacles from which few return. Creatures that wander the desolation of Carceri often construct prisons in his image. Those who rob others of their freedom offer prayers to him in cellars and other subterranean domains, and many creatures who live in the darkness below worship him and seek his guidance.\n\nTorog remains banished within an unknown sliver of the Far Realm that now borders the deepest pits of the Underdark, where the boundaries between worlds grow thin and birth terrible abominations bent on subjugation.\n\nDepiction\n\nThe Crawling King is rendered as a swollen, malformed worm that slithers through the dark below, with a screaming, hairless human head at the helm and three arms carving through the lightless rock.\n\nEnemies\n\nPelor and Raei defeated Torog during the Calamity by luring their nemesis above ground. Pelor pierced Torog's tenebrous body with ten thousand lances of sunlight, and the Everlight imprisoned him beyond the boundaries of Exandria. The tears of pain and anger the Crawling King shed burned through Exandria, and his faithful fled into these tunnels to escape their enemies' holy light.\n\nCommandments of Torog\n\n• Seek and exalt places where no light touches.\n\n• Revel in the pain you inflict on others, and relish the pain you suffer yourself as an offering to Torog.\n\n• Imprison those who cannot resist you, and drag all life into the darkness."},
  ["creature.torogar-steelfist.bgdia2014"]={title="Torogar Steelfist",subtitle="Criatura - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 112\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 168 (16d10 + 80)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 17 | CON 20 | INT 8 | WIS 9 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nGoring Rush\n\nImmediately after using the Dash action, Torogar can make one melee attack with his horns.\n\nLabyrinthine Recall\n\nTorogar can perfectly recall any path he has traveled.\n\nRage (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nAs a bonus action, Torogar can enter a rage that lasts for 1 minute. The rage ends early if Torogar is knocked unconscious or if his turn ends and he hasn't attacked a hostile creature or taken damage since his last turn. While raging, Torogar gains the following benefits:\n\nHe has advantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws.\n\nHe deals an extra 3 damage when he hits a target with a melee weapon attack.\n\nHe has resistance to bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing damage.\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nTorogar wears BGDIA and a belt of fire giant strength. Without the belt, his Strength is 21. He also carries a BGDIA.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nTorogar makes three attacks: two with his scimitars and one with his horns.\n\nScimitar\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (2d6 + 7) slashing damage, or 17 (2d6 + 10) slashing damage while raging, plus 3 (1d6) fire damage from the gauntlets of flaming fury.\n\nHorns\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h16 (2d8 + 7) piercing damage, or 19 (2d8 + 10) piercing damage while raging."},
  ["item.torpor.dmg2014"]={title="Torpor",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 258\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA creature subjected to this poison must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or become poisoned for 4d6 hours. The poisoned creature is incapacitated."},
  ["item.torpor.xdmg2024"]={title="Torpor",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 91\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA creature subjected to Torpor poison must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or have the XPHB condition for 4d6 hours. The creature's XPHB is halved while the creature is XPHB in this way."},
  ["creature.tortle.mpmm2014"]={title="Tortle",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 244\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 22 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 10 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 13 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Aquan, Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nHold Breath\n\nThe tortle can hold its breath for 1 hour.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaw\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage, or 6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage if used with two hands in melee.\n\nLight Crossbow\n\nrw 2 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. h4 (1d8) piercing damage.\n\nShell Defense\n\nThe tortle withdraws into its shell. Until it emerges, it gains a +4 bonus to AC and has advantage on Strength and Constitution saving throws. While in its shell, the tortle is prone, its speed is 0 and can't increase, it has disadvantage on Dexterity saving throws, it can't take reactions, and the only action it can take is a bonus action to emerge."},
  ["species.tortle.mpmm2014"]={title="Tortle",subtitle="Especie - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\nSize\n\nYou are Medium or Small. You choose the size when you select this race.\n\nClaws\n\nYou have claws that you can use to make unarmed strikes. When you hit with them, the strike deals 1d6 + your Strength modifier slashing damage, instead of the bludgeoning damage normal for an unarmed strike.\n\nHold Breath\n\nYou can hold your breath for up to 1 hour.\n\nNatural Armor\n\nYour shell provides you a base AC of 17 (your Dexterity modifier doesn't affect this number). You can't wear light, medium, or heavy armor, but if you are using a shield, you can apply the shield's bonus as normal.\n\nNature's Intuition\n\nThanks to your mystical connection to nature, you gain proficiency with one of the following skills of your choice: Animal Handling, Medicine, Nature, Perception, Stealth, or Survival.\n\nShell Defense\n\nYou can withdraw into your shell as an action. Until you emerge, you gain a +4 bonus to your AC, and you have advantage on Strength and Constitution saving throws. While in your shell, you are prone, your speed is 0 and can't increase, you have disadvantage on Dexterity saving throws, you can't take reactions, and the only action you can take is a bonus action to emerge from your shell."},
  ["creature.tortle.mtf2014"]={title="Tortle",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 242\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 22 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 10 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 13 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Aquan, Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nHold Breath\n\nThe tortle can hold its breath for 1 hour.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaws\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nQuarterstaff\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage, or 6 (1d8 + 2) bludgeoning damage if used with two hands.\n\nLight Crossbow\n\nrw 2 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. h4 (1d8) piercing damage.\n\nShell Defense\n\nThe tortle withdraws into its shell. Until it emerges, it gains a +4 bonus to AC and has advantage on Strength and Constitution saving throws. While in its shell, the tortle is prone, its speed is 0 and can't increase, it has disadvantage on Dexterity saving throws, it can't take reactions, and the only action it can take is a bonus action to emerge."},
  ["species.tortle.ttp2014"]={title="Tortle",subtitle="Especie - TTP - 2014",body="Pagina: 3\n\nThe Tortle Package is considered part of Xanathar's Guide to Everything for Adventurers League character creation.\n\nAge\n\nYoung tortles crawl for a few weeks after birth before learning to walk on two legs. They reach adulthood by the age of 15 and live an average of 50 years.\n\nAlignment\n\nTortles tend to lead orderly, ritualistic lives. They develop customs and routines, becoming more set in their ways as they age. Most are lawful good. A few can be selfish and greedy, tending more toward evil, but it's unusual for a tortle to shuck off order in favor of chaos.\n\nSize\n\nTortle adults stand 5 to 6 feet tall and average 450 pounds. Their shells account for roughly one-third of their weight. Your size is Medium.\n\nClaws\n\nYour claws are natural weapons, which you can use to make unarmed strikes. If you hit with them, you deal slashing damage equal to 1d4 + your Strength modifier, instead of bludgeoning damage normal for an unarmed strike.\n\nHold Breath\n\nYou can hold your breath for up to 1 hour at a time. Tortles aren't natural swimmers, but they can remain underwater for some time before needing to come up for air.\n\nNatural Armor\n\nDue to your shell and the shape of your body, you are ill-suited to wearing armor. Your shell provides ample protection, however; it gives you a base AC of 17 (your Dexterity modifier doesn't affect this number). You gain no benefit from wearing armor, but if you are using a shield, you can apply the shield's bonus as normal.\n\nShell Defense\n\nYou can withdraw into your shell as an action. Until you emerge, you gain a +4 bonus to AC, and you have advantage on Strength and Constitution saving throws. While in your shell, you are prone, your speed is 0 and can't increase, you have disadvantage on Dexterity saving throws, you can't take reactions, and the only action you can take is a bonus action to emerge from your shell.\n\nSurvival Instinct\n\nYou gain proficiency in the Survival skill. Tortles have finely honed survival instincts.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Aquan and Common."},
  ["creature.tortle-druid.mpmm2014"]={title="Tortle Druid",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 244\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 10 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 15 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Aquan, Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nHold Breath\n\nThe tortle can hold its breath for 1 hour.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe tortle makes four Claw attacks or two Nature's Wrath attacks.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nNature's Wrath\n\nrs 4 to hit, range 90 ft., one target. h9 (2d6 + 2) damage of a type chosen by the tortle: cold, fire, lightning, or thunder.\n\nShell Defense\n\nThe tortle withdraws into its shell. Until it emerges, it gains a +4 bonus to AC and has advantage on Strength and Constitution saving throws. While in its shell, the tortle is prone, its speed is 0 and can't increase, it has disadvantage on Dexterity saving throws, it can't take reactions, and the only action it can take is a bonus action to emerge."},
  ["creature.tortle-druid.mtf2014"]={title="Tortle Druid",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 242\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 10 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 15 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Aquan, Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nHold Breath\n\nThe tortle can hold its breath for 1 hour.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaws\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nQuarterstaff\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage, or 6 (1d8 + 2) bludgeoning damage if used with two hands.\n\nShell Defense\n\nThe tortle withdraws into its shell. Until it emerges, it gains a +4 bonus to AC and has advantage on Strength and Constitution saving throws. While in its shell, the tortle is prone, its speed is 0 and can't increase, it has disadvantage on Dexterity saving throws, it can't take reactions, and the only action it can take is a bonus action to emerge."},
  ["creature.tosh-starling-levels-1-4.kftgv2014"]={title="Tosh Starling (Levels 1-4)",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.tosh-starling-levels-5-8.kftgv2014"]={title="Tosh Starling (Levels 5-8)",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.tosh-starling-levels-9-11.kftgv2014"]={title="Tosh Starling (Levels 9-11)",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["item.totem.phb2014"]={title="Totem",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["feature.totem-spirit.phb2014.barbarian.totem-warrior.3"]={title="Totem Spirit",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\nAt 3rd level, when you adopt this path, you choose a totem spirit and gain its feature. You must make or acquire a physical totem object—an amulet or similar adornment—that incorporates fur or feathers, claws, teeth, or bones of the totem animal. At your option, you also gain minor physical attributes that are reminiscent of your totem spirit. For example, if you have a bear totem spirit, you might be unusually hairy and thick-skinned, or if your totem is the eagle, your eyes turn bright yellow.\n\nYour totem animal might be an animal related to those listed here but more appropriate to your homeland. For example, you could choose a hawk or vulture in place of an eagle."},
  ["feature.totemic-attunement.phb2014.barbarian.totem-warrior.14"]={title="Totemic Attunement",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\nAt 14th level, you gain a magical benefit based on a totem animal of your choice. You can choose the same animal you selected previously or a different one."},
  ["feat.touch-of-death.rhw2014"]={title="Touch of Death",subtitle="Feat - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 35\n\nDeathly power resides within you, bursting out at the slightest provocation. You gain the following features.\n\nDeath Touch\n\nYou learn the XPHB spell and can cast it without spell components. Necrotic damage you deal with this spell ignores XPHB. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for this spell (choose when you select this feat).\n\nPull of the Grave\n\nYou have XPHB on XPHB."},
  ["feature.touch-of-death.scag2014.monk.long-death.3"]={title="Touch of Death",subtitle="Caracteristica - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 130\n\nStarting when you choose this tradition at 3rd level, your study of death allows you to extract vitality from another creature as it nears its demise. When you reduce a creature within 5 feet of you to 0 hit points, you gain temporary hit points equal to your Wisdom modifier + your monk level (minimum of 1 temporary hit point)."},
  ["charoption.touch-of-death.vrgr2014"]={title="Touch of Death",subtitle="Opcao de Personagem - VRGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 26\n\nYour touch is pain, harming whoever you come in contact with. The deathly power within you is beyond your control, afflicting any who touch your bare skin. By the same token, you can deliver death to your enemies with your touch.\n\nRoll on or choose an option from the Deadly Touch table to determine how this Dark Gift presents itself. Additionally, you gain the traits that follow.\n\nd6 | Manifestation\n\n1 | Your body is alchemically or biologically altered, infusing you with deadly chemicals.\n\n2 | The magic of a slighted druid or fey makes small plants wither and insects die in your presence.\n\n3 | You're the harbinger of a grim prophecy. Any creature your touch damages is marked with a temporary scar of a group, fiend, deity, or other force that takes an interest in you.\n\n4 | You survived a near-death experience—but shouldn't have. Ever since, death and ill omens follow you.\n\n5 | You are out of sync with time or reality. Anything you touch is warped by the distortion.\n\n6 | Every time you touch a creature, you hear the laughter of someone you once harmed.\n\nDeath Touch\n\nYou can focus your deadly touch against your foes. As an action, make one unarmed strike. On a hit, the target takes an additional 1d10 necrotic damage. This damage increases by 1d10 when you reach 5th level (2d10), 11th level (3d10), and 17th level (4d10).\n\nInescapable Death\n\nWhen you hit a target with an attack roll and deal necrotic damage, you ignore the target's resistance to that damage.\n\nWithering Contact\n\nWhen you start your turn grappling a creature or grappled by it, the creature takes 1d10 necrotic damage."},
  ["feature.touch-of-the-long-death.scag2014.monk.long-death.17"]={title="Touch of the Long Death",subtitle="Caracteristica - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 130\n\nStarting at 17th level, your touch can channel the energy of death into a creature. As an action, you touch one creature within 5 feet of you, and you expend 1 to 10 ki points. The target must make a Constitution saving throw, and it takes 2d10 necrotic damage per ki point spent on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["feat.tough.phb2014"]={title="Tough",subtitle="Feat - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 170\n\nYour hit point maximum increases by an amount equal to twice your level when you gain this feat. Whenever you gain a level thereafter, your hit point maximum increases by an additional 2 hit points."},
  ["creature.tough.xmm2024"]={title="Tough",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 307\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 32 (5d8 + 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 12 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 11\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe tough has XPHB on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the tough's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally doesn't have the XPHB condition.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMace\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage.\n\nHeavy Crossbow\n\nr 3, range 100/400 ft. h6 (1d10 + 1) Piercing damage."},
  ["feat.tough.xphb2024"]={title="Tough",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 202\n\nYour XPHB maximum increases by an amount equal to twice your character level when you gain this feat. Whenever you gain a character level thereafter, your XPHB maximum increases by an additional 2 XPHB."},
  ["creature.tough-boss.xmm2024"]={title="Tough Boss",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 307\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 82 (11d8 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 11 | WIS 10 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus one other language\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe tough has XPHB on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the tough's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally doesn't have the XPHB condition.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe tough makes two attacks, using Warhammer or Heavy Crossbow in any combination.\n\nWarhammer\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h12 (2d8 + 3) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, the tough pushes the target up to 10 feet straight away from itself.\n\nHeavy Crossbow\n\nr 4, range 100/400 ft. h13 (2d10 + 2) Piercing damage."},
  ["item.tourmaline.dmg2014"]={title="Tourmaline",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA transparent pale green, blue, brown, or red gemstone."},
  ["item.tourmaline.xdmg2024"]={title="Tourmaline",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA pale green, blue, brown, or red gemstone."},
  ["creature.tower-hand.qftis2014"]={title="Tower Hand",subtitle="Criatura - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 217\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 22 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nUnarmored Defense\n\nWhile the tower hand is wearing no armor and wielding no shield, its AC includes its Wisdom modifier.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe tower hand makes two Unarmed Strike attacks, two Dart attacks, or one of each.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage.\n\nDart\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 20/60 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nDeflect Missile\n\nIn response to being hit by a ranged weapon attack, the tower hand deflects the missile. The damage it takes from the attack is reduced by 7 (1d10 + 2)."},
  ["creature.tower-sage.qftis2014"]={title="Tower Sage",subtitle="Criatura - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 217\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 10/13\n\nPV: 22 (5d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 10 | CON 10 | INT 16 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus any three languages\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe tower sage makes two Arcane Burst attacks and can use Starry Radiance if available.\n\nArcane Burst\n\nms,rs 5 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft., one target. h8 (1d10 + 3) radiant damage.\n\nStarry Radiance {@recharge 5}\n\nDazzling light bursts from the tower sage's fingertips in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in that area must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or have the blinded condition until the end of the tower sage's next turn."},
  ["creature.traag-draconian.mcv2dc2014"]={title="Traag Draconian",subtitle="Criatura - MCV2DC - 2014",body="Pagina: 13\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 68 (8d10 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 10 | CON 17 | INT 6 | WIS 8 | CHA 9\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBlood Frenzy\n\nThe draconian has advantage on melee attack rolls against any creature that doesn't have all its hit points.\n\nControlled Fall\n\nIf the draconian falls and isn't incapacitated, it subtracts up to 50 feet from the fall when calculating the fall's damage.\n\nDeath Throes\n\nIf the draconian is reduced to 0 hit points, its body erupts into sludge that fills a 10-foot-radius sphere. Each creature within that area must succeed on a 14 Dexterity saving throw or be covered in the sludge for 1 minute. While covered in the sludge, a creature's speed is halved. A creature can use its action to scrape the sludge off itself or another creature within 5 feet of itself.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe draconian makes two Claw attacks.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h14 (2d8 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nFlaming Carnage {@recharge 5}\n\nThe draconian indulges its rage, wreathing itself in fire and moving up to its speed. The draconian can enter creatures' spaces during this move. During this movement, when the draconian enters a creature's space, the creature must make a 14 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 22 (4d10) fire damage and is knocked prone. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and is pushed to the nearest space out of the draconian's path. A creature can be affected by this draconian's Flaming Carnage only once during a turn.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nViolent Retaliation\n\nIf a creature within 10 feet of the draconian hits it with an attack, the draconian can make one Claw attack against that creature. If the Claw attack hits, it deals an additional 4 (1d8) slashing damage."},
  ["feature.training-in-war-and-song.frhof2014.wizard.bladesinger.3"]={title="Training in War and Song",subtitle="Caracteristica - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\nYou gain proficiency with all Melee Martial weapons that don't have the XPHB or XPHB property. You can use a Melee weapon with which you have proficiency as a XPHB for your Wizard spells.\n\nYou also gain proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB."},
  ["feature.training-in-war-and-song-bladesinging.tce2014.wizard.bladesinging.2"]={title="Training in War and Song (Bladesinging)",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.trance-of-order.tce2014.sorcerer.clockwork-soul.14"]={title="Trance of Order",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 68\n\n14th-level Clockwork Soul feature\n\nYou gain the ability to align your consciousness to the endless calculations of Mechanus. As a bonus action, you can enter this state for 1 minute. For the duration, attack rolls against you can't benefit from advantage, and whenever you make an attack roll, an ability check, or a saving throw, you can treat a roll of 9 or lower on the d20 as a 10.\n\nOnce you use this bonus action, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest, unless you spend 5 sorcery points to use it again."},
  ["feature.trance-of-order.xphb2024.sorcerer.clockwork.14"]={title="Trance of Order",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["magicitem.tranquil-rod-of-the-honed-mind.au2014"]={title="Tranquil Rod of the Honed Mind",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 133\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias"},
  ["feature.tranquility.phb2014.monk.open-hand.11"]={title="Tranquility",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 79\n\nBeginning at 11th level, you can enter a special meditation that surrounds you with an aura of peace. At the end of a long rest, you gain the effect of a sanctuary spell that lasts until the start of your next long rest (the spell can end early as normal). The saving throw DC for the spell equals 8 + your Wisdom modifier + your proficiency bonus."},
  ["creature.transcendent-order-conduit.mpp2014"]={title="Transcendent Order Conduit",subtitle="Criatura - MPP - 2014",body="Pagina: 62\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 97 (15d8 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 19 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 18 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus one more language\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nInstinctive Reflexes\n\nThe conduit has advantage on initiative rolls, and it can't have disadvantage on attack rolls.\n\nUnarmored Defense\n\nWhile the conduit is wearing no armor and wielding no shield, its AC includes its Wisdom modifier.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe conduit makes three Unarmed Strike attacks.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, the conduit can choose one of the following additional effects (up to once per turn each):\n\n• Incapacitate The target must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or have the incapacitated condition until the end of the conduit's next turn.\n\n• Push The target is pushed up to 10 feet horizontally away from the conduit.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nDeflect Attack\n\nIn response to being hit by an attack roll, the conduit partially deflects the blow. The damage the conduit takes from the attack is reduced by 1d10.\n\nDon't Be There\n\nWhen the conduit must make a saving throw, it can move up to half its speed without provoking opportunity attacks. If its new position moves it out of range or otherwise makes it impossible to be targeted by the effect, the conduit avoids the effect entirely."},
  ["creature.transcendent-order-instinct.mpp2014"]={title="Transcendent Order Instinct",subtitle="Criatura - MPP - 2014",body="Pagina: 62\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 49 (9d8 + 9)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 16 | CON 12 | INT 10 | WIS 16 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus one more language\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nUnarmored Defense\n\nWhile the instinct is wearing no armor and wielding no shield, its AC includes its Wisdom modifier.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe instinct makes three Unarmed Strike attacks.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) bludgeoning damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nDeflect Blow\n\nIn response to being hit by a melee attack roll, the instinct partially deflects the blow. The damage the instinct takes from the attack is reduced by 1d6."},
  ["spell.transfix.au2014"]={title="Transfix",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 7 - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 44\n\nFor the duration, your appearance becomes otherworldly and alluring. One creature of your choice that you can see within 60 feet of you must succeed on a Charisma saving throw or have the XPHB condition for the duration.\n\nWhile XPHB, the target has the XPHB condition, and if the target is more than 5 feet away from you, it moves on its turn toward you by the most direct route, trying to get within 5 feet of you. If the XPHB creature ends its turn within 5 feet of you, it takes 4d8 Psychic damage.\n\nThe target doesn't avoid XPHB when moving toward you, but before moving into damaging terrain (such as lava or a pit), the target repeats the save, ending the spell on itself on a success.\n\nUntil the spell ends, you can take a XPHB action on subsequent turns to target another creature, but you can't target a creature again if it has succeeded on a save against this casting of the spell."},
  ["feat.transmutation-adept.au2014"]={title="Transmutation Adept",subtitle="Feat - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 32\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nAdditional Spells\n\nYour prowess allows you to always have certain spells at the ready. When you have spell slots of a level specified in the Transmutation Adept Spells table, you thereafter always have the spells listed for that level and lower prepared.\n\nMagical Augmentation\n\nOn your turn when you cast a spell from the Transmutation school using a spell slot, your XPHB increases by a number of feet equal to five times the level of spell slot expended. This increase lasts until the end of the turn.\n\nSpell Slot Level | Spell\n\n1 | XPHB\n\n2 | XPHB\n\n3 | XPHB\n\n4 | XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB"},
  ["feature.transmutation-savant.au2014.wizard.transmuter.3"]={title="Transmutation Savant",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 19\n\nChoose two spells, each of which must be no higher than level 2, and add them to your spellbook for free.\n\nIn addition, whenever you gain access to a new level of spell slots in this class, you can add one spells to your spellbook for free. The chosen spell must be of a level for which you have spell slots."},
  ["feature.transmutation-savant.phb2014.wizard.transmutation.2"]={title="Transmutation Savant",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\nBeginning when you select this school at 2nd level, the gold and time you must spend to copy a transmutation spell into your spellbook is halved."},
  ["spell.transmute-rock.xge2024"]={title="Transmute Rock",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 169\n\nYou choose an area of stone or mud that you can see that fits within a 40-foot cube and is within range, and choose one of the following effects.\n\nTransmute Rock to Mud\n\nNonmagical rock of any sort in the area becomes an equal volume of thick, flowing mud that remains for the spell's duration.\n\nThe ground in the spell's area becomes muddy enough that creatures can sink into it. Each foot that a creature moves through the mud costs 4 feet of movement, and any creature on the ground when you cast the spell must make a Strength saving throw. A creature must also make the saving throw when it moves into the area for the first time on a turn or ends its turn there. On a failed save, a creature sinks into the mud and is restrained, though it can use an action to end the restrained condition on itself by pulling itself free of the mud.\n\nIf you cast the spell on a ceiling, the mud falls. Any creature under the mud when it falls must make a Dexterity saving throw. A creature takes 4d8 bludgeoning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nTransmute Mud to Rock\n\nNonmagical mud or quicksand in the area no more than 10 feet deep transforms into soft stone for the spell's duration. Any creature in the mud when it transforms must make a Dexterity saving throw. On a successful save, a creature is shunted safely to the surface in an unoccupied space. On a failed save, a creature becomes restrained by the rock. A restrained creature, or another creature within reach, can use an action to try to break the rock by succeeding on a 20 Strength check or by dealing damage to it. The rock has AC 15 and 25 hit points, and it is immune to poison and psychic damage."},
  ["feat.transmuted-anatomy.au2014"]={title="Transmuted Anatomy",subtitle="Feat - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 28\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nLengthened Stride\n\nYour XPHB increases by 5 feet.\n\nResilient Anatomy\n\nYou have XPHB on saving throws against effects that would compel you to shape-shift against your will. Additionally, when you fail a Constitution saving throw, you can take a XPHB to roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to the save, potentially turning the failure into a success. You can use this benefit a number of times equal to your XPHB, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB."},
  ["optionalfeature.transmuted-spell.tce2014"]={title="Transmuted Spell",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 66\n\nWhen you cast a spell that deals a type of damage from the following list, you can spend 1 sorcery point to change that damage type to one of the other listed types: acid, cold, fire, lightning, poison, thunder."},
  ["optionalfeature.transmuted-spell.xphb2024"]={title="Transmuted Spell",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 142\n\nWhen you cast a spell that deals a type of damage from the following list, you can spend 1 Sorcery Point to change that damage type to one of the other listed types: Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison, Thunder."},
  ["subclass.transmuter.au2014.wizard.transmuter.0"]={title="Transmuter",subtitle="Subclasse - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 19\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Transmutation Savant\n\nPagina: 19\n\nChoose two spells, each of which must be no higher than level 2, and add them to your spellbook for free.\n\nIn addition, whenever you gain access to a new level of spell slots in this class, you can add one spells to your spellbook for free. The chosen spell must be of a level for which you have spell slots.\n\nNivel 3 - Transmuter\n\nPagina: 19\n\nTransform Energy and Matter\n\nYou study spells that modify energy and matter—to you, the world is eminently mutable. Using your magic, you become a smith at reality's forge.\n\nSome Transmuters are tinkerers and pranksters. Others seek the power to make and destroy worlds.\n\nNivel 3 - Transmuter's Stone\n\nPagina: 19\n\nWhen you finish a XPHB, you can create a magic stone that lasts until you use this feature again. The stone is a Tiny object, and you can use it as a XPHB for your Wizard spells. A creature with the stone in its possession gains proficiency in Constitution saving throws and one of the following benefits, which you choose when you create the stone. You can change the stone's benefit when you cast a spells using a spell slot.\n\nDarkvision\n\nThe bearer gains XPHB with a range of 60 feet or increases the range of its XPHB by 60 feet.\n\nResistance\n\nThe bearer gains XPHB to Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, Poison, or Thunder damage (your choice each time you choose this benefit).\n\nSpeed\n\nThe bearer's XPHB increases by 10 feet.\n\nNivel 3 - Transmuter's Stone\n\nNivel 3 - Wondrous Alteration\n\nPagina: 19\n\nYou always have the XPHB spell prepared and can cast it once without expending a spell slot. You regain the ability to cast it in this way when you finish a XPHB.\n\nWhile under the effects of XPHB, you gain an additional benefit for each of its options.\n\nAquatic Adaptation\n\nWhile underwater, you can take the XPHB action as a XPHB.\n\nChange Appearance\n\nYou have XPHB on Charisma (XPHB) checks.\n\nNatural Weapons\n\nThe damage of your new growth increases to 2d6 damage of the type associated with the growth. You also have XPHB on Constitution saving throws to maintain XPHB.\n\nNivel 3 - Wondrous Alteration\n\nNivel 6 - Empowered Transmutation\n\nPagina: 20\n\nWhen you use a spell slot to cast a spells that doesn't make an attack roll or force a saving throw, such as XPHB or XPHB, you can increase the spell's effective level by 1.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 6 - Empowered Transmutation\n\nNivel 10 - Potent Stone\n\nPagina: 20\n\nYour Transmuter's Stone is more versatile. When you create your Transmuter's Stone, you can choose up to two benefits. You can choose each option other than Resistance only once. If you choose Resistance twice, you must choose different damage types. You can change either or both benefits when you cast a spells using a spell slot.\n\nIn addition, the following are now among your benefit options for Transmuter's Stone.\n\nMighty Build\n\nThe bearer has XPHB on Strength saving throws. The bearer also counts as one size larger when determining its carrying capacity.\n\nTremorsense\n\nThe bearer gains XPHB with a range of 30 feet.\n\nNivel 10 - Shape-Shifter\n\nPagina: 20\n\nYou always have the XPHB spell prepared and can cast it once without expending a spell slot. You regain the ability to cast it in this way when you finish a XPHB.\n\nIn addition, when you target yourself with the spell, you can modify the spell to gain the benefits below. Once you modify the spell using this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nGame Statistics\n\nIn addition to retaining the features specified in the spell, you retain your memories and ability to communicate. You also retain your Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores; proficiencies; class features; and feats.\n\nTransmute Spells\n\nWhile shape-shifted, you can cast spells, but only spells that don't have a Material component that has a specified cost or that is consumed by the spell.\n\nNivel 10 - Shape-Shifter\n\nNivel 14 - Master Transmuter\n\nPagina: 20\n\nWhile you carry your Transmuter's Stone, you can take a XPHB action to consume the reserve of transmutation magic stored inside and choose one of the following benefits. After you use the stone in this way, it crumbles to dust. You can prevent the stone from crumbling by expending a level 7+ spell slot as part of the XPHB action you take using this feature.\n\nMajor Transformation\n\nYou can transmute one nonmagical object—no larger than a 10-foot XPHB or eight connected 5-foot Cubes—into another nonmagical object of similar size and mass and of equal or lesser value. You must spend 10 minutes handling the object to transform it.\n\nPanacea\n\nYou touch a creature as part of this XPHB action, and the target regains a number of XPHB equal to half its XPHB maximum (round down). The target is cured of all magical contagions, and any curses affecting the target are lifted, including the target's XPHB to a cursed item. If the target has the XPHB or XPHB condition, those conditions end.\n\nRestore Life\n\nYou cast the XPHB spell without expending a spell slot, using the stone in place of the required Material components.\n\nRestore Youth\n\nYou touch one willing creature as part of this XPHB action, and the target's XPHB level, if any, decreases to 0, and it permanently appears 3d10 years younger, to a minimum of young adulthood.\n\nNivel 14 - Master Transmuter"},
  ["feature.transmuter.au2014.wizard.transmuter.3"]={title="Transmuter",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 19\n\nTransform Energy and Matter\n\nYou study spells that modify energy and matter—to you, the world is eminently mutable. Using your magic, you become a smith at reality's forge.\n\nSome Transmuters are tinkerers and pranksters. Others seek the power to make and destroy worlds."},
  ["creature.transmuter.vgm2014"]={title="Transmuter",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 218\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 12/15\n\nPV: 40 (9d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 14 | CON 11 | INT 17 | WIS 12 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any four languages\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nTransmuter's Stone\n\nThe transmuter carries a magic stone it crafted that grants its bearer one of the following effects:\n\nDarkvision out to a range of 60 feet\n\nAn extra 10 feet of speed while the bearer is unencumbered\n\nProficiency with Constitution saving throws\n\nResistance to acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder damage (transmuter's choice whenever the transmuter chooses this benefit)\n\nIf the transmuter has the stone and casts a transmutation spell of 1st level or higher, it can change the effect of the stone.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nQuarterstaff\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h2 (1d6 - 1) bludgeoning damage, or 3 (1d8 - 1) bludgeoning damage if used with two hands."},
  ["creature.transmuter-archmage.au2014"]={title="Transmuter Archmage",subtitle="Criatura - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 139\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 220 (40d8 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 16 | CON 12 | INT 20 | WIS 15 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common plus five other languages\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe archmage has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nSlow (2/Day)\n\nProtective Magic (3/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe archmage makes four Arcane Burst attacks.\n\nArcane Burst\n\nm,r 10, reach 5 ft. or range 150 ft. h27 (4d10 + 5) Force damage."},
  ["creature.transmuter-wizard.mpmm2014"]={title="Transmuter Wizard",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 265\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 12/15\n\nPV: 49 (11d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 14 | CON 11 | INT 17 | WIS 12 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any four languages\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nTransmuter's Stone\n\nThe transmuter carries a magic stone it crafted. The stone grants it one of the following benefits while bearing the stone; the transmuter chooses the benefit at the end of each long rest:\n\n• Darkvision\n\n• Resilience\n\n• Resistance\n\n• Speed\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe transmuter makes three Arcane Burst attacks.\n\nArcane Burst\n\nms,rs 6 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft., one target. h19 (3d10 + 3) acid damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nTransmute {@recharge 4}\n\nThe transmuter casts alter self or changes the benefit of Transmuter's Stone if bearing the stone."},
  ["feature.transmuter-s-stone.au2014.wizard.transmuter.3"]={title="Transmuter's Stone",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.transmuter-s-stone.phb2014.wizard.transmutation.6"]={title="Transmuter's Stone",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\nStarting at 6th level, you can spend 8 hours creating a transmuter's stone that stores transmutation magic. You can benefit from the stone yourself or give it to another creature. A creature gains a benefit of your choice as long as the stone is in the creature's possession. When you create the stone, choose the benefit from the following options:\n\n• Darkvision out to a range of 60 feet, as described in chapter 8.\n\n• An increase to speed of 10 feet while the creature is unencumbered.\n\n• Proficiency in Constitution saving throws.\n\n• Resistance to acid, cold, fire, lightning, or thunder damage (your choice whenever you choose this benefit).\n\nEach time you cast a transmutation spell of 1st level or higher, you can change the effect of your stone if the stone is on your person.\n\nIf you create a new transmuter's stone, the previous one ceases to function."},
  ["spell.transport-via-plants.phb2014"]={title="Transport via Plants",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 283\n\nThis spell creates a magical link between a Large or larger inanimate plant within range and another plant, at any distance, on the same plane of existence. You must have seen or touched the destination plant at least once before. For the duration, any creature can step into the target plant and exit from the destination plant by using 5 feet of movement."},
  ["spell.transport-via-plants.xphb2024"]={title="Transport via Plants",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 334\n\nThis spell creates a magical link between a Large or larger inanimate plant within range and another plant, at any distance, on the same plane of existence. You must have seen or touched the destination plant at least once before. For the duration, any creature can step into the target plant and exit from the destination plant by using 5 feet of movement."},
  ["creature.trapper.mpmm2014"]={title="Trapper",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 245\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 68 (8d10 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, climb: 20\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 10 | CON 17 | INT 2 | WIS 13 | CHA 4\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nIf the trapper is motionless on a floor, wall, or ceiling at the start of combat, it has advantage on its initiative roll. Moreover, if a creature hasn't observed the trapper move or act, that creature must succeed on a 18 Intelligence (Investigation) check to discern that the trapper isn't part of the floor, wall, or ceiling.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe trapper can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSmother\n\nOne Large or smaller creature within 10 feet of the trapper must succeed on a 13 Dexterity saving throw or be grappled (escape 14). Until the grapple ends, the target takes 13 (3d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage plus 3 (1d6) acid damage at the start of each of its turns. While grappled in this way, the target is restrained, blinded, and deprived of air. The trapper can smother only one creature at a time."},
  ["creature.trapper.vgm2014"]={title="Trapper",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 194\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 85 (10d10 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, climb: 10\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 10 | CON 17 | INT 2 | WIS 13 | CHA 4\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the trapper is attached to a ceiling, floor, or wall and remains motionless, it is almost indistinguishable from an ordinary section of ceiling, floor, or wall. A creature that can see it and succeeds on a 20 Intelligence (Investigation) or Intelligence (Nature) check can discern its presence.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe trapper can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSmother\n\nOne Large or smaller creature within 5 feet of the trapper must succeed on a 14 Dexterity saving throw or be grappled (escape 14). Until the grapple ends, the target takes 17 (4d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage plus 3 (1d6) acid damage at the start of each of its turns. While grappled in this way, the target is restrained, blinded, and at risk of suffocating. The trapper can smother only one creature at a time."},
  ["charoption.trauma-survivor.vrgr2014"]={title="Trauma Survivor",subtitle="Opcao de Personagem - VRGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 32\n\nYou survived. Whatever it was, you made it through, and you can help others do the same. People view you as an expert on the traumatic situation you faced—be it a specific sort of violence, illness, or otherwise. You are aware of nonmagical recovery techniques, common resources, and misinformation. You know how to speak to sympathetic doctors, clergy, and local leaders and can convince them to shelter one person (other than yourself) at a modest lifestyle for up to one month."},
  ["magicitem.travel-alchemical-kit.ai2014"]={title="Travel Alchemical Kit",subtitle="Item Magico - AI - 2014",body="Pagina: 30\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nAlso at rank 3, Head Office provides you with a travel alchemical kit—an uncommon magic item containing miniaturized versions of both phb and a phb (glass vials, a mortar and pestle, chemicals, and a glass stirring rod). You gain proficiency with a phb as part of this upgrade.\n\nYou can use this magical kit as long as it is on your person, with no need to draw or stow it. If you are ever searched, finding your travel alchemical kit requires a successful 20 Intelligence (Investigation) or Wisdom (Insight) check."},
  ["feature.travel-along-the-tree.xphb2024.barbarian.world-tree.14"]={title="Travel Along the Tree",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["charoption.traveler.vrgr2014"]={title="Traveler",subtitle="Opcao de Personagem - VRGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 32\n\nYou come from somewhere else, a place others couldn't begin to understand. Perhaps your home is a unique corner of the Land of the Mists or another world entirely. In any case, you and other travelers have shared experiences. You can find a place to hide, rest, or recuperate among sympathetic trading caravans, itinerant families, or displaced groups, so long as you don't present yourself as a danger. Such groups will hide you from the law or anyone searching for you, though they won't risk their lives for you. Additionally, you can tell whether an object you can see and touch is from your homeland with near perfect accuracy."},
  ["item.traveler-s-clothes.phb2014"]={title="Traveler's Clothes",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.traveler-s-clothes.xphb2024"]={title="Traveler's Clothes",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 225\n\nRaridade: none\n\nTraveler's Clothes are resilient garments designed for travel in various environments."},
  ["magicitem.traveler-s-pearl.au2014"]={title="Traveler's Pearl",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 124\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nBy using a command word while holding this pearl, you can cast the XPHB spell from it. Once this property is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["reward.traveling-snacks.au2014"]={title="Traveling Snacks",subtitle="Recompensa - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 113\n\nAfter spending a XPHB in your Bastion, you gain a magical Charm that lasts for 7 days or until you use it. The Charm allows you to cast XPHB once without expending a spell slot."},
  ["creature.traxigor.bgdia2014"]={title="Traxigor",subtitle="Criatura - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / T\n\nSTR 3\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Dwarvish, Gnomish, Halfling, Troglodyte"},
  ["feat.treacherous-allure.abh2014"]={title="Treacherous Allure",subtitle="Feat - ABH - 2014",body="Pagina: 10\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nEnchanting Presence\n\nYou always have the XPHB spell prepared. You can cast it without a spell slot, and you must finish a XPHB before you can cast it in this way again. You can also cast it using spell slots you have of the appropriate level. Your spellcasting ability for the spell is the ability increased by this feat.\n\nInevitable Betrayal\n\nYou have XPHB on attack rolls against creatures with the XPHB condition."},
  ["creature.treant.mm2014"]={title="Treant",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 289\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / H\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 138 (12d12 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 8 | CON 21 | INT 12 | WIS 16 | CHA 12\n\nIdiomas: Common, Druidic, Elvish, Sylvan\n\nResistencias: bludgeoning, piercing\n\nVulnerabilidades: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the treant remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from a normal tree.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe treant deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe treant makes two slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h16 (3d6 + 6) bludgeoning damage.\n\nRock\n\nrw 10 to hit, range 60/180 ft., one target. h28 (4d10 + 6) bludgeoning damage.\n\nAnimate Trees (1/Day)\n\nThe treant magically animates one or two trees it can see within 60 feet of it. These trees have the same statistics as a treant, except they have Intelligence and Charisma scores of 1, they can't speak, and they have only the Slam action option. An animated tree acts as an ally of the treant. The tree remains animate for 1 day or until it dies; until the treant dies or is more than 120 feet from the tree; or until the treant takes a bonus action to turn it back into an inanimate tree. The tree then takes root if possible."},
  ["creature.treant.xmm2024"]={title="Treant",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 308\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / H\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 138 (12d12 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 8 | CON 21 | INT 12 | WIS 16 | CHA 12\n\nIdiomas: Common, Druidic, Elvish, Sylvan\n\nResistencias: bludgeoning, piercing\n\nVulnerabilidades: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe treant deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe treant makes two Slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nm 10, reach 5 ft. h16 (3d6 + 6) Bludgeoning damage.\n\nHail of Bark\n\nr 10, range 180 ft. h28 (4d10 + 6) Piercing damage.\n\nAnimate Trees (1/Day)\n\nThe treant magically animates up to two trees it can see within 60 feet of itself. Each tree uses the Treant stat block, except it has Intelligence and Charisma scores of 1, it can't speak, and it lacks this action. The tree takes its turn immediately after the treant on the same XPHB count, and it obeys the treant. A tree remains animate for 1 day or until it dies, the treant dies, or it is more than 120 feet from the treant. The tree then takes root if possible."},
  ["creature.treant-sapling.wbtw2014"]={title="Treant Sapling",subtitle="Criatura - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 36\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 45 (6d10 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 8 | CON 15 | INT 12 | WIS 12 | CHA 10\n\nIdiomas: Common, Druidic, Elvish, Sylvan\n\nResistencias: bludgeoning, piercing\n\nVulnerabilidades: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nIf the treant is motionless at the start of combat, it has advantage on its initiative roll. Moreover, if a creature hasn't observed the treant move or act, that creature must succeed on a 18 Intelligence (Investigation) check to discern that the treant is animate.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe treant makes two Slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d10 + 3) bludgeoning damage.\n\nRock\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 20/60 ft., one target. h14 (2d10 + 3) bludgeoning damage.\n\nAnimate Trees (1/Day)\n\nThe treant magically animates one or two trees it can see within 60 feet of it. These trees have the same statistics as an awakened tree (see the Monster Manual), except they can't speak. An animated tree acts as an ally of the treant. The tree remains animate for 1 day or until it dies, until the treant dies or is more than 120 feet from the tree, or until the treant takes a bonus action to turn it back into an inanimate tree. The tree then takes root if possible."},
  ["creature.treant-totem-elemental.psx2014"]={title="Treant Totem Elemental",subtitle="Criatura - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 38\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["item.treasure-chest-crafted-of-exotic-wood-with-gold-fittings-and-opals-brazen-coalition.psx2014"]={title="Treasure chest crafted of exotic wood with gold fittings and opals (Brazen Coalition)",subtitle="Item - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 25\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["object.trebuchet.dmg2014"]={title="Trebuchet",subtitle="Objeto - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 256\n\nA trebuchet is a powerful catapult that throws its payload in a high arc, so it can hit targets behind cover.\n\nBefore the trebuchet can be fired, it must be loaded and aimed. It takes two actions to load the weapon, two actions to aim it, and one action to fire it.\n\nA trebuchet typically hurls a heavy stone. However, it can launch other kinds of projectiles, such as barrels of oil or sewage, with different effects."},
  ["object.trebuchet.xdmg2024"]={title="Trebuchet",subtitle="Objeto - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 97\n\nA Trebuchet is a catapult that throws its payload in a high arc so it can hit targets behind walls. Loading a Trebuchet requires two XPHB actions, and aiming it requires two more XPHB actions. Then a crew member can take the Trebuchet Stone action."},
  ["creature.tree-blight.cos2014"]={title="Tree Blight",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 230\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / H\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 92 (8d12 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 10 | CON 20 | INT 6 | WIS 10 | CHA 3\n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nIdiomas: understands Common and Druidic but doesn't speak\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, deafened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the blight remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from a dead tree.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe blight deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe blight makes one Branch attack and one Grasping Root attack.\n\nBranch\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h16 (3d6 + 6) bludgeoning damage.\n\nGrasping Root\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 15 ft., one creature not grappled by the blight. hThe target is grappled (escape 15). Until the grapple ends, the target takes 9 (1d6 + 6) bludgeoning damage at the start of each of its turns. The root has AC 15 and can be severed by dealing 6 slashing damage or more to it at once. Cutting the root doesn't hurt the blight, but ends the grapple.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature grappled by the blight. h19 (3d8 + 6) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.tree-blight.xmm2024"]={title="Tree Blight",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 44\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / H\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 115 (10d12 + 50)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 10 | CON 20 | INT 6 | WIS 10 | CHA 3\n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common and Druidic but can't speak\n\nImunidades a condicoes: deafened\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe blight makes two Branch attacks and uses Grasping Root.\n\nBranch\n\nm 9, reach 15 ft. h16 (3d6 + 6) Bludgeoning damage.\n\nGrasping Root\n\nstr 17, one Large or smaller creature the blight can see within 15 feet. actSaveFail The target is pulled up to 10 feet straight toward the blight and has the XPHB condition (escape 16) from one of six roots. Until the grapple ends, the target takes 13 (2d6 + 6) Bludgeoning damage at the start of each of its turns.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nGnash\n\ndex 17, one creature XPHB by the blight. actSaveFail 19 (3d8 + 6) Piercing damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage."},
  ["spell.tree-stride.phb2014"]={title="Tree Stride",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 283\n\nYou gain the ability to enter a tree and move from inside it to inside another tree of the same kind within 500 feet. Both trees must be living and at least the same size as you. You must use 5 feet of movement to enter a tree. You instantly know the location of all other trees of the same kind within 500 feet and, as part of the move used to enter the tree, can either pass into one of those trees or step out of the tree you're in. You appear in a spot of your choice within 5 feet of the destination tree, using another 5 feet of movement. If you have no movement left, you appear within 5 feet of the tree you entered.\n\nYou can use this transportation ability once per round for the duration. You must end each turn outside a tree."},
  ["spell.tree-stride.xphb2024"]={title="Tree Stride",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 335\n\nYou gain the ability to enter a tree and move from inside it to inside another tree of the same kind within 500 feet. Both trees must be living and at least the same size as you. You must use 5 feet of movement to enter a tree. You instantly know the location of all other trees of the same kind within 500 feet and, as part of the move used to enter the tree, can either pass into one of those trees or step out of the tree you're in. You appear in a spot of your choice within 5 feet of the destination tree, using another 5 feet of movement. If you have no movement left, you appear within 5 feet of the tree you entered.\n\nYou can use this transportation ability only once on each of your turns. You must end each turn outside a tree."},
  ["creature.treefolk.mcv4ec2014"]={title="Treefolk",subtitle="Criatura - MCV4EC - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / L\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 171 (18d10 + 72)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 12 | CON 18 | INT 10 | WIS 20 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Druidic, Sylvan\n\nResistencias: bludgeoning, piercing\n\nVulnerabilidades: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPlant Camouflage\n\nThe treefolk has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks it makes in forest terrain.\n\nTree Stride\n\nOnce on each of its turns, the treefolk can use 10 feet of its movement to step magically into one living tree within 5 feet of itself and emerge from a second living tree within 60 feet of itself that it can see, appearing in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the second tree. Both trees must be at least as large as the treefolk.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe treefolk makes two Crushing Vine attacks, two Nightshade Bolt attacks, or one of each.\n\nCrushing Vine\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h25 (3d12 + 6) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it has the grappled condition (escape 18). While grappled, the creature also has the restrained condition. The treefolk can grapple up to six creatures this way.\n\nNightshade Bolt\n\nrs 9 to hit, range 60 ft., one target. h33 (6d10) poison damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nOaken Boon\n\nThe treefolk blesses one creature other than itself that it can see within 60 feet of itself with the might and wisdom of the forest. While blessed in this way, a creature can use the treefolk's Tree Stride trait and gains 5 (2d4) temporary hit points at the start of each of its turns. This blessing lasts for 1 minute, until the treefolk has the incapacitated condition, or until the treefolk uses this bonus action again."},
  ["creature.trench-giant.psz2014"]={title="Trench Giant",subtitle="Criatura - PSZ - 2014",body="Pagina: 30\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.trenzia.wdmm2014"]={title="Trenzia",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 32\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nResistencias: fire, necrotic, piercing\n\nImunidades: lightning, cold, poison\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nTrenzia uses Lightning Ray twice.\n\nFire Ray\n\nrs 5 to hit, range 30 ft., one target. h10 (3d6) lightning damage."},
  ["creature.trepsin.hotdq2014"]={title="Trepsin",subtitle="Criatura - HotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 63\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / L\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 84 (8d10 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 13 | CON 20 | INT 7 | WIS 9 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Giant\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Smell\n\nThe troll has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe troll regains 10 hit points at the start of its turn. If the troll takes acid or fire damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of the troll's next turn. The troll dies only if it starts its turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe troll attacks five times, once with its bite and four times with its claws. If two or more claws hit the same target, the troll rends the target, dealing an extra 2d6 slashing damage.\n\nBite\n\nmw +7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw +7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.tressym.bgdia2014"]={title="Tressym",subtitle="Criatura - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 241\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.tressym.skt2014"]={title="Tressym",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 242\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / T\n\nCR: 0\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 5 (2d4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 30, fly: 40\n\nSTR 3 | DEX 15 | CON 10 | INT 11 | WIS 12 | CHA 12\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common but can't speak\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDetect Invisibility\n\nWithin 60 feet of the tressym, magical invisibility fails to conceal anything from the tressym's sight.\n\nKeen Smell\n\nThe tressym has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.\n\nPoison Sense\n\nThe tressym can detect whether a substance is poisonous by taste, touch, or smell.\n\nFamiliar\n\nWith the DM's permission, a person who casts the find familiar spell can choose to conjure a tressym instead of a normal cat.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaws\n\nmw 0 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h1 slashing damage."},
  ["creature.tri-flower-frond.toa2014"]={title="Tri-flower Frond",subtitle="Criatura - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 234\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 9 | WIS 13 | CHA 9\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft.\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, deafened, exhaustion, prone\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe tri-flower frond uses its orange blossom, then its yellow blossom, and then its red blossom.\n\nOrange Blossom\n\nThe tri-flower frond chooses one creature it can see within 5 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 11 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned for 1 hour. While poisoned in this way, the target is unconscious. At the end of each minute, the poisoned target can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nYellow Blossom\n\nThe tri-flower frond chooses one creature it can see within 5 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 11 Dexterity saving throw, or it is covered with corrosive sap and takes 5 acid damage at the start of each of its turns. Dousing the target with water reduces the acid damage by 1 point per pint or flask of water used.\n\nRed Blossom\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h2 (1d4) piercing damage, and the target is grappled (escape 11). Until this grapple ends, the target takes 5 (2d4) poison damage at the start of each of its turns. The red blossom can grapple only one target at a time. Another creature within reach of the tri-flower frond can use its action to end the grapple on the target."},
  ["creature.tribal-warrior.mm2014"]={title="Tribal Warrior",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 350\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 11 | CON 12 | INT 8 | WIS 11 | CHA 8\n\nIdiomas: any one language\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe warrior has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the warrior's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h4 (1d6 + 1) piercing damage, or 5 (1d8 + 1) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack."},
  ["creature.tribal-warrior-spore-servant.idrotf2014"]={title="Tribal Warrior Spore Servant",subtitle="Criatura - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 52\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 11 | CON 12 | INT 2 | WIS 6 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, frightened, paralyzed"},
  ["creature.triceratops.mm2014"]={title="Triceratops",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 80\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / H\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 95 (10d12 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 9 | CON 17 | INT 2 | WIS 11 | CHA 5\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nTrampling Charge\n\nIf the triceratops moves at least 20 feet straight toward a creature and then hits it with a gore attack on the same turn, that target must succeed on a 13 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone. If the target is prone, the triceratops can make one stomp attack against it as a bonus action.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nGore\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h24 (4d8 + 6) piercing damage.\n\nStomp\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one prone creature. h22 (3d10 + 6) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.triceratops.xmm2024"]={title="Triceratops",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 372\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / H\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 114 (12d12 + 36)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 9 | CON 17 | INT 2 | WIS 11 | CHA 5\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe triceratops makes two Gore attacks.\n\nGore\n\nm 9, reach 5 ft. h19 (2d12 + 6) Piercing damage. If the target is Huge or smaller and the triceratops moved 20+ feet straight toward it immediately before the hit, the target takes an extra 9 (2d8) Piercing damage and has the XPHB condition."},
  ["subclass.trickery-domain.phb2014.cleric.trickery.0"]={title="Trickery Domain",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 1 - Blessing of the Trickster\n\nPagina: 62\n\nStarting when you choose this domain at 1st level, you can use your action to touch a willing creature other than yourself to give it advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks. This blessing lasts for 1 hour or until you use this feature again.\n\nNivel 1 - Trickery Domain\n\nPagina: 62\n\nGods of trickery—such as Tymora, Beshaba, Greyhawk, Eberron, Nonhuman, and Norse—are mischief-makers and instigators who stand as a constant challenge to the accepted order among both gods and mortals. They're patrons of thieves, scoundrels, gamblers, rebels, and liberators. Their clerics are a disruptive force in the world, puncturing pride, mocking tyrants, stealing from the rich, freeing captives, and flouting hollow traditions. They prefer subterfuge, pranks, deception, and theft rather than direct confrontation.\n\nAt each indicated cleric level, you add the listed spells to your spells prepared.\n\nCleric Level | Spells\n\n1st | charm person, disguise self\n\n3rd | mirror image, pass without trace\n\n5th | blink, dispel magic\n\n7th | dimension door, polymorph\n\n9th | dominate person, modify memory\n\nNivel 2 - Channel Divinity: Invoke Duplicity\n\nPagina: 62\n\nStarting at 2nd level, you can use your Channel Divinity to create an illusory duplicate of yourself.\n\nAs an action, you create a perfect illusion of yourself that lasts for 1 minute, or until you lose your concentration (as if you were concentration on a spell). The illusion appears in an unoccupied space that you can see within 30 feet of you. As a bonus action on your turn, you can move the illusion up to 30 feet to a space you can see, but it must remain within 120 feet of you.\n\nFor the duration, you can cast spells as though you were in the illusion's space, but you must use your own senses. Additionally, when both you and your illusion are within 5 feet of a creature that can see the illusion, you have advantage on attack rolls against that creature, given how distracting the illusion is to the target.\n\nNivel 2 - Channel Divinity: Invoke Duplicity\n\nNivel 3 - Blessing of the Trickster\n\nPagina: 75\n\nAs a XPHB action, you can choose yourself or a willing creature within 30 feet of yourself to have XPHB on Dexterity (XPHB) checks. This blessing lasts until you finish a XPHB or you use this feature again.\n\nNivel 3 - Blessing of the Trickster\n\nNivel 3 - Channel Divinity: Invoke Duplicity\n\nNivel 3 - Invoke Duplicity\n\nPagina: 75\n\nAs a XPHB, you can expend one use of your Channel Divinity to create a perfect visual illusion of yourself in an unoccupied space you can see within 30 feet of yourself. The illusion is intangible and doesn't occupy its space. It lasts for 1 minute, but it ends early if you dismiss it (no action required) or have the XPHB condition. The illusion is animated and mimics your expressions and gestures. While it persists, you gain the following benefits.\n\nCast Spells\n\nYou can cast spells as though you were in the illusion's space, but you must use your own senses.\n\nDistract\n\nWhen both you and your illusion are within 5 feet of a creature that can see the illusion, you have XPHB on attack rolls against that creature, given how distracting the illusion is to the target.\n\nMove\n\nAs a XPHB, you can move the illusion up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see that is within 120 feet of yourself.\n\nNivel 3 - Invoke Duplicity\n\nNivel 3 - Trickery Domain\n\nNivel 3 - Trickery Domain\n\nPagina: 75\n\nMake Mischief and Challenge Authority\n\nThe Trickery Domain offers magic of deception, illusion, and stealth. Clerics who wield this magic are a disruptive force in the world, puncturing pride, mocking tyrants, freeing captives, and flouting hollow traditions. They prefer subterfuge and pranks to direct confrontation.\n\nGods of trickery are mischief-makers and instigators who stand as a constant challenge to the accepted order among both gods and mortals. They embody the forces of change and social upheaval, and they're patrons of thieves, scoundrels, gamblers, rebels, and liberators. Religious orders that operate in secret, especially those that seek to undermine oppressive governments or hierarchies, also draw on the power of the Trickery Domain.\n\nNivel 3 - Trickery Domain Spells\n\nPagina: 76\n\nYour connection to this divine domain ensures you always have certain spells ready. When you reach a Cleric level specified in the Trickery Domain Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nCleric Level | Prepared Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\nNivel 6 - Channel Divinity: Cloak of Shadows\n\nPagina: 62\n\nStarting at 6th level, you can use your Channel Divinity to vanish.\n\nAs an action, you become invisible until the end of your next turn. You become visible if you attack or cast a spell.\n\nNivel 6 - Trickster's Transposition\n\nPagina: 76\n\nWhenever you take the XPHB to create or move the illusion of your Invoke Duplicity, you can teleport, swapping places with the illusion.\n\nNivel 6 - Trickster's Transposition\n\nNivel 8 - Blessed Strikes\n\nPagina: 30\n\n{@i 8th-level cleric tce, which replaces the Divine Strike feature\n\nYou are blessed with divine might in battle. When a creature takes damage from one of your cantrips or weapon attacks, you can also deal 1d8 radiant damage to that creature. Once you deal this damage, you can't use this feature again until the start of your next turn.\n\nNivel 8 - Divine Strike\n\nPagina: 62\n\nAt 8th level, you gain the ability to infuse your weapon strikes with poison—a gift from your deity. Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can cause the attack to deal an extra 1d8 poison damage to the target. When you reach 14th level, the extra damage increases to 2d8.\n\nNivel 8 - Divine Strike\n\nNivel 17 - Improved Duplicity\n\nPagina: 62\n\nAt 17th level, you can create up to four duplicates of yourself, instead of one, when you use Invoke Duplicity. As a bonus action on your turn, you can move any number of them up to 30 feet, to a maximum range of 120 feet.\n\nNivel 17 - Improved Duplicity\n\nPagina: 76\n\nThe illusion of your Invoke Duplicity has grown more powerful in the following ways.\n\nShared Distraction\n\nWhen you and your allies make attack rolls against a creature within 5 feet of the illusion, the attack rolls have XPHB.\n\nHealing Illusion\n\nWhen the illusion ends, you or a creature of your choice within 5 feet of it regains a number of XPHB equal to your Cleric level.\n\nNivel 17 - Improved Duplicity"},
  ["feature.trickery-domain.phb2014.cleric.trickery.1"]={title="Trickery Domain",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 62\n\nGods of trickery—such as Tymora, Beshaba, Greyhawk, Eberron, Nonhuman, and Norse—are mischief-makers and instigators who stand as a constant challenge to the accepted order among both gods and mortals. They're patrons of thieves, scoundrels, gamblers, rebels, and liberators. Their clerics are a disruptive force in the world, puncturing pride, mocking tyrants, stealing from the rich, freeing captives, and flouting hollow traditions. They prefer subterfuge, pranks, deception, and theft rather than direct confrontation.\n\nAt each indicated cleric level, you add the listed spells to your spells prepared.\n\nCleric Level | Spells\n\n1st | charm person, disguise self\n\n3rd | mirror image, pass without trace\n\n5th | blink, dispel magic\n\n7th | dimension door, polymorph\n\n9th | dominate person, modify memory"},
  ["feature.trickery-domain.phb2014.cleric.trickery.3"]={title="Trickery Domain",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["subclass.trickery-domain.xphb2024.cleric.trickery.0"]={title="Trickery Domain",subtitle="Subclasse - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 75\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 1 - Blessing of the Trickster\n\nPagina: 62\n\nStarting when you choose this domain at 1st level, you can use your action to touch a willing creature other than yourself to give it advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks. This blessing lasts for 1 hour or until you use this feature again.\n\nNivel 1 - Trickery Domain\n\nPagina: 62\n\nGods of trickery—such as Tymora, Beshaba, Greyhawk, Eberron, Nonhuman, and Norse—are mischief-makers and instigators who stand as a constant challenge to the accepted order among both gods and mortals. They're patrons of thieves, scoundrels, gamblers, rebels, and liberators. Their clerics are a disruptive force in the world, puncturing pride, mocking tyrants, stealing from the rich, freeing captives, and flouting hollow traditions. They prefer subterfuge, pranks, deception, and theft rather than direct confrontation.\n\nAt each indicated cleric level, you add the listed spells to your spells prepared.\n\nCleric Level | Spells\n\n1st | charm person, disguise self\n\n3rd | mirror image, pass without trace\n\n5th | blink, dispel magic\n\n7th | dimension door, polymorph\n\n9th | dominate person, modify memory\n\nNivel 2 - Channel Divinity: Invoke Duplicity\n\nPagina: 62\n\nStarting at 2nd level, you can use your Channel Divinity to create an illusory duplicate of yourself.\n\nAs an action, you create a perfect illusion of yourself that lasts for 1 minute, or until you lose your concentration (as if you were concentration on a spell). The illusion appears in an unoccupied space that you can see within 30 feet of you. As a bonus action on your turn, you can move the illusion up to 30 feet to a space you can see, but it must remain within 120 feet of you.\n\nFor the duration, you can cast spells as though you were in the illusion's space, but you must use your own senses. Additionally, when both you and your illusion are within 5 feet of a creature that can see the illusion, you have advantage on attack rolls against that creature, given how distracting the illusion is to the target.\n\nNivel 2 - Channel Divinity: Invoke Duplicity\n\nNivel 3 - Blessing of the Trickster\n\nPagina: 75\n\nAs a XPHB action, you can choose yourself or a willing creature within 30 feet of yourself to have XPHB on Dexterity (XPHB) checks. This blessing lasts until you finish a XPHB or you use this feature again.\n\nNivel 3 - Blessing of the Trickster\n\nNivel 3 - Channel Divinity: Invoke Duplicity\n\nNivel 3 - Invoke Duplicity\n\nPagina: 75\n\nAs a XPHB, you can expend one use of your Channel Divinity to create a perfect visual illusion of yourself in an unoccupied space you can see within 30 feet of yourself. The illusion is intangible and doesn't occupy its space. It lasts for 1 minute, but it ends early if you dismiss it (no action required) or have the XPHB condition. The illusion is animated and mimics your expressions and gestures. While it persists, you gain the following benefits.\n\nCast Spells\n\nYou can cast spells as though you were in the illusion's space, but you must use your own senses.\n\nDistract\n\nWhen both you and your illusion are within 5 feet of a creature that can see the illusion, you have XPHB on attack rolls against that creature, given how distracting the illusion is to the target.\n\nMove\n\nAs a XPHB, you can move the illusion up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see that is within 120 feet of yourself.\n\nNivel 3 - Invoke Duplicity\n\nNivel 3 - Trickery Domain\n\nNivel 3 - Trickery Domain\n\nPagina: 75\n\nMake Mischief and Challenge Authority\n\nThe Trickery Domain offers magic of deception, illusion, and stealth. Clerics who wield this magic are a disruptive force in the world, puncturing pride, mocking tyrants, freeing captives, and flouting hollow traditions. They prefer subterfuge and pranks to direct confrontation.\n\nGods of trickery are mischief-makers and instigators who stand as a constant challenge to the accepted order among both gods and mortals. They embody the forces of change and social upheaval, and they're patrons of thieves, scoundrels, gamblers, rebels, and liberators. Religious orders that operate in secret, especially those that seek to undermine oppressive governments or hierarchies, also draw on the power of the Trickery Domain.\n\nNivel 3 - Trickery Domain Spells\n\nPagina: 76\n\nYour connection to this divine domain ensures you always have certain spells ready. When you reach a Cleric level specified in the Trickery Domain Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nCleric Level | Prepared Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\nNivel 6 - Channel Divinity: Cloak of Shadows\n\nPagina: 62\n\nStarting at 6th level, you can use your Channel Divinity to vanish.\n\nAs an action, you become invisible until the end of your next turn. You become visible if you attack or cast a spell.\n\nNivel 6 - Trickster's Transposition\n\nPagina: 76\n\nWhenever you take the XPHB to create or move the illusion of your Invoke Duplicity, you can teleport, swapping places with the illusion.\n\nNivel 6 - Trickster's Transposition\n\nNivel 8 - Blessed Strikes\n\nPagina: 30\n\n{@i 8th-level cleric tce, which replaces the Divine Strike feature\n\nYou are blessed with divine might in battle. When a creature takes damage from one of your cantrips or weapon attacks, you can also deal 1d8 radiant damage to that creature. Once you deal this damage, you can't use this feature again until the start of your next turn.\n\nNivel 8 - Divine Strike\n\nPagina: 62\n\nAt 8th level, you gain the ability to infuse your weapon strikes with poison—a gift from your deity. Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can cause the attack to deal an extra 1d8 poison damage to the target. When you reach 14th level, the extra damage increases to 2d8.\n\nNivel 8 - Divine Strike\n\nNivel 17 - Improved Duplicity\n\nPagina: 62\n\nAt 17th level, you can create up to four duplicates of yourself, instead of one, when you use Invoke Duplicity. As a bonus action on your turn, you can move any number of them up to 30 feet, to a maximum range of 120 feet.\n\nNivel 17 - Improved Duplicity\n\nPagina: 76\n\nThe illusion of your Invoke Duplicity has grown more powerful in the following ways.\n\nShared Distraction\n\nWhen you and your allies make attack rolls against a creature within 5 feet of the illusion, the attack rolls have XPHB.\n\nHealing Illusion\n\nWhen the illusion ends, you or a creature of your choice within 5 feet of it regains a number of XPHB equal to your Cleric level.\n\nNivel 17 - Improved Duplicity"},
  ["feature.trickery-domain.xphb2024.cleric.trickery.3"]={title="Trickery Domain",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 75\n\nMake Mischief and Challenge Authority\n\nThe Trickery Domain offers magic of deception, illusion, and stealth. Clerics who wield this magic are a disruptive force in the world, puncturing pride, mocking tyrants, freeing captives, and flouting hollow traditions. They prefer subterfuge and pranks to direct confrontation.\n\nGods of trickery are mischief-makers and instigators who stand as a constant challenge to the accepted order among both gods and mortals. They embody the forces of change and social upheaval, and they're patrons of thieves, scoundrels, gamblers, rebels, and liberators. Religious orders that operate in secret, especially those that seek to undermine oppressive governments or hierarchies, also draw on the power of the Trickery Domain."},
  ["feature.trickery-domain-spells.xphb2024.cleric.trickery.3"]={title="Trickery Domain Spells",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 76\n\nYour connection to this divine domain ensures you always have certain spells ready. When you reach a Cleric level specified in the Trickery Domain Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nCleric Level | Prepared Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB"},
  ["optionalfeature.trickster-s-escape.xge2024"]={title="Trickster's Escape",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 57\n\nYou can cast freedom of movement once on yourself without expending a spell slot. You regain the ability to do so when you finish a long rest."},
